Part 2 (balance re-run): AbilityUsageSoak with GAIDEN_ABILITY_PARTY=campaign GAIDEN_ABILITY_STAGE=greenvalley-01 confirms Green Valley I is still a severe dip for the real 3-hero start at difficulty 10 after GG-T311+GG-T306 land (smart 6.2%->25% after a3f/a5d0c0e''s wave-3 trim, casual 0%->0%; d5/d1 improved more, see a5d0c0e''s commit message for the full before/after table). Root cause (forced Guard eating 35-50% of the small party''s actions, GG-T311''s ActionFits gate) tracked separately on GG-T316 since it needs a party-size-aware mechanic change, not a content trim. Endless sanity run (harness.py endless) stayed crash/stall-free but reproduced the same forced-Guard signature on a full 5-hero demo party too (note on this ticket); stopped short of a full win-rate tally given session time since it doesn''t change the GG-T313 verdict. Commits: 3ea4f07, a5d0c0e. Follow-ups: GG-T316 (forced-Guard/party-size balance), GG-T317 (off-stage banner, cosmetic).', 312, NULL);
1) LedgerSweeper.cs:~211 - a closed-but-still-claimed ticket falls through the Claimed&&!Closed guard into the lease-expiry check, so Judge deletes its scratch dir on lease expiry, contradicting the documented invariant ''a ticket still claimed keeps its scratch whatever its lease says''.
2) ToolCallText.cs Program() ~57-78 - naive whitespace tokenization of the command line misidentifies the program name when a quoted path contains a space (e.g. ''& "C:\Program Files\dotnet\dotnet.exe" build'' returns ''Program'' instead of dotnet).
3) QuicksaveCapture.cs TryReadCode ~27-30 - updatedAt is parsed with DateTimeStyles.RoundtripKind without AssumeUniversal, so an offset-less timestamp parses as Unspecified and ToUniversalTime() then shifts it by the local UTC offset on non-UTC machines, unlike ResourceLedger/TranscriptReader which use AdjustToUniversal|AssumeUniversal.
4) BackupRestore.cs MatchDumps ~99-103 - looks up a project''s roster entry by the sanitized on-disk folder name, but byProject is keyed by the roster''s unsanitized project name; SqliteBackup.SanitizeFileName replaces invalid filename chars when writing the backup folder but restore never reverses this, so a project name containing such a character (e.g. ''App:Test'' -> folder ''App_Test'') is silently skipped on restore even though it exists in the roster.
5) PrerequisiteService.cs ~262 and ~285 - Process.Kill(entireProcessTree:true) is wrapped in a catch that only catches InvalidOperationException; Kill() can also throw Win32Exception (e.g. access denied, or a race with the process naturally exiting), which escapes uncaught and can crash the bootstrap/health thread calling EnsureHard/EnsureAiCli.
6) DuplicationAudit.cs ~77 - ''if (ids.Count < 2 || ids.Count > MaxFilesPerWindow) continue;'' (MaxFilesPerWindow = 12) silently drops every fingerprint window shared by more than 12 files, so a snippet copied into more than 12 of the ~26 MindAttic repos is never reported as duplicated even though it is the most-duplicated case in the scan - this one needs a product decision on whether/how to raise or remove the cap before fixing; flag as needs-human-input if so on closer look.', 'already done: items 1-5 landed (64162dbf, M.ORCH-T2332..T2334); item 6 is M.ORCH-T2335', 2327, NULL);
