**Goal.** One message exchange for every MindAttic app and machine: MindAttic.Relay, NATS + JetStream, with shared
Protocol Buffers contracts, one client library, an outbox, credentials and TLS from day one. Then the hub-and-spoke plan
(members'' own machines joined into one Orchestrator, everyone''s CLIs visible and shareable, single-machine mode
unchanged) is built on top of it instead of on hand-made sockets, outboxes and heartbeats.

**Order** (priority and `requires` links enforce it):

1. Relay foundation: server as a service, contracts, client, security, outbox.
2. First users: AppBus between Orchestrator.Desktop and Tickets.Desktop; KdpPublish''s `prose.book.published` (ASIN).
3. Across machines: leaf nodes with JetStream domains, device credentials and auth callout, monitoring.
4. Hub and spoke, phases 0 to 6, rewritten on Relay.

**Origin.** This epic supersedes Orchestrator epic M.ORCH-T1145 (hub and spoke, from spike M.ORCH-T1127). Its 18
phase tickets and M.TIX-T173 moved here as M.RLY tickets; each new ticket `supersedes` its old one, and the old ones
closed wont-do with "moved to M.RLY-Tn". The full pre-Relay design stays in MindAttic.Orchestrator
`docs/design/hub-and-spoke/` and in M.ORCH-T1145''s description; where it conflicts with docs/design/relay.md in MindAttic.Relay, Relay''s design wins.', 'Runs after MAUI: every ticket here waits for the v2.0.0 release (M.ORCH-T1240).

EPIC: MindAttic.Relay, one message exchange for every MindAttic app and machine (NATS + JetStream), and hub and spoke built on it: members'' machines joined into one Orchestrator, everyone''s CLIs visible and shareable, single-machine mode unchanged.

**Rules:**
- App-facing work is written once into the shared Presentation layer, so all four shells (WPF and Maui of Orchestrator and Tickets) get it together.
- UI work lands in both shells in one commit (M.ORCH-T1238).
- The named-pipe bus stays as a permanent fallback: nothing depends on Relay to keep working.

