<!-- What goes wrong, and how to see it. -->

## Cause

<!-- Why it happens, once known. -->

## Test

<!-- The test that fails before the fix and passes after. -->', '## Symptom

obj_phalanx never trails sparks in the rebuild. Nothing in Core or presentation raises or draws
an effect for it.

## Cause

`R:\Projects\_PRE_2022\_PRE_2021\_PRE_2020\GameMaker\gmlHARE\HARE.gmx\objects\obj_phalanx.object.gmx`''s
Step event ends with an unconditional `effect_create_below(ef_spark, x, y, 0, c_gold)` every step
while moving (after the distance_to_object(player)/move_towards_point block). `PhalanxEnemy.StepEvent`
in `Assets/Unity.Rea.Hare/Core/Enemies/PhalanxEnemy.cs` has no equivalent: it never emits a spark
event, so this is a missing Core feature, not just an unwired presentation event (unlike
U.HARE-T110''s dagger/mine cases, where Core already raised the event and only the drawing was
missing). Needs: a new EnemyEvent type (e.g. PhalanxSparked) raised once a step from
PhalanxEnemy.StepEvent, a case in EnemyDirector.PlayEvent calling
`GmlEffects.CreateBelow(GmlEffectKind.Spark, at, 0, <gold>)`, and Core tests asserting the event
fires every step while the phalanx moves.

## Test

A new Core test on PhalanxEnemy (e.g. in Tests/Core.Tests) asserting a PhalanxSparked event (or
equivalent) is emitted each step, and an EditMode/PlayMode check that EnemyDirector.PlayEvent
draws it via GmlEffects.');

Profile: a named binding of concrete stores to the existing ISettingsStore<T>/ICredentialStore abstractions. The tab list and every field, per app, is defined once against that app''s own settings type and is Profile-agnostic; switching the active Profile (one global switch in Desktop) swaps which backend answers every tab''s Load/Save at once. ''Desktop'' Profile binds to the existing local AppData file stores, unchanged. ''Azure'' Profile binds to Key Vault (secrets) + Azure App Configuration (plain settings), resolved once per app via an interactive resource picker (Azure.ResourceManager) and cached locally -- no connection strings or resource IDs ever re-entered. A future platform is just another Profile with new store implementations; no UI rework.

Load/Save on the Azure Profile replaces the Azure portal entirely: Load pulls current values into the same fields the Desktop Profile uses, Save writes them back. Key Vault secrets are versioned (Save creates a new version under the same name); App Configuration key-values update in place.

Azure SDK dependencies (Azure.Identity, Azure.ResourceManager.*, Azure.Security.KeyVault.Secrets, Azure.Data.AppConfiguration) live only in Vault.Desktop, never in the shared MindAttic.Vault core package (M.VALT-LAW-5 unaffected). Every write to Azure happens as the operator''s own authenticated identity from Desktop, not from a deployed app or a running service -- production apps stay read-only against Azure config (M.VALT-LAW-4 unaffected, no amendment needed).', '**Code name LAMP. Full approved plan: `MindAttic.Vault/docs/rfc/0003-lamp.md`.** Supersedes RFC 0002 (M.VALT-T26, wont-do).

One native WPF app, **MindAttic.Vault.Desktop**, never network-exposed, is the only place any MindAttic app''s settings or keys are edited. No web-hosted settings UI is ever built.

- **Profiles**: `Desktop` (local AppData files) and `Azure` (App Configuration holds every name and plain value; Key Vault holds secret values via Key Vault references). Same tabs and fields in every Profile; Load/Save on Azure replaces the Azure portal. More Profiles later = one new class.
- **App tabs are generated** from each app''s `settings.manifest.json` (written from `[SettingsApp]`/`[Setting]`/`[UsesCredential]` attributes on the app''s settings class). No app UI code runs inside Desktop.
- **Name/Value everywhere**, IConfiguration-style: `{AppId}:{Property}`, `Llm:{provider}:ApiKeys:{keyName}`, `{AppId}:Keys:{provider}` = ordered key names (first = active, rest = fallbacks).
- **Keys**: one shared named list per provider (provider catalog with aliases), managed only on the Keys tab; apps pick an active key + fallbacks on their own tab; no per-app secret copies (existing scoped copies are imported).
- **Failover**: `KeySelector` tries active then fallbacks; 401/403 marks a key failed, 429 cools it down; key health is shared machine-wide and shown in Desktop.
- **First run**: each app seeds defaults from its settings class (`LoadOrSeed`); new users only bring keys (Get Started checklist).
- Local keys stay plain text (no DPAPI). Per-user / per-universe / CMS data stays in its app.
- Remembered state, audit log, single instance (`--app <id>` from each app''s cog), folder-ACL check, `MaSecretBox`.

Delivered together, built in dependency order: Vault core → Components → Vault.Desktop → Azure Profile → every app. Every child ticket is linked `part-of` this one.');

As V, I want twin pistols and a Max Payne style trench coat added to my inventory when the mod loads, so I have the signature loadout without hunting for it.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Mod load grants exactly one trench coat garment item and two pistol-type weapon items to V''s inventory, once per save.
- [ ] Items reskin existing game archetypes/TweakDB records (via TweakXL), not placeholder debug items, so they equip and render normally.
- [ ] Grant logic is idempotent: reloading the same save, or restarting CET, never re-grants duplicates.
- [ ] Verify in-game: load a save with the mod active, open inventory, confirm both pistols and the coat are present and equippable; reload the save and confirm no duplicates appeared.');

As V, I want the mod to recognize a dedicated Shootdodge input combo (aim held + jump + a movement direction) without misfiring during normal play, so the move triggers only when I mean it to.

## Acceptance

- [ ] CET input listener detects aim (ADS) held + jump pressed + non-zero movement input within the same short window.
- [ ] The combo does not fire on jump alone, aim alone, or movement alone.
- [ ] A debug overlay (ImGui) logs each detected trigger with a timestamp, for manual verification before any dive mechanic is wired to it.
- [ ] Verify in-game: ~1 minute of ordinary jumping/aiming/moving with the overlay open produces zero false triggers; pressing the real combo logs exactly one trigger.');

As V, I want the mod''s state machine to show my current Shootdodge state (NONE/DIVING/AIRBORNE/PRONE/GETUP) at all times, so every later mechanic is built and debugged against one known state.

## Acceptance

- [ ] ImGui debug overlay always displays the current state: NONE, DIVING, AIRBORNE, PRONE, or GETUP.
- [ ] State defaults to NONE on load and on any uncaught edge case (never gets stuck in a non-NONE state with no mechanic driving it).
- [ ] All transitions are defined in one centralized table/function, not scattered ad hoc checks across the script.
- [ ] Verify in-game: state overlay reads NONE throughout a normal play session (the T5 combo is detected but not yet wired to any transition).');

As V, I want the input combo to launch me into a horizontal dive toward my aim direction, so I leave the ground the way Max Payne does.

## Acceptance

- [ ] A detected T5 combo while in state NONE transitions to DIVING and applies an impulse that sends V airborne, horizontally, toward the camera/aim direction.
- [ ] The initial leap reuses an existing game animation/impulse (a custom .animgraph dive pose is explicitly out of scope here; open question captured in docs/DESIGN.md for a later pass).
- [ ] The dive cannot be re-triggered mid-air: the state guard only allows the transition from NONE.
- [ ] Verify in-game: trigger the combo from standing; V leaves the ground toward the aim direction and the overlay reads DIVING; repeating the combo mid-air does nothing.');

As V, I want world time to slow dramatically for the duration of the dive, so the moment feels like Max Payne''s bullet-time instead of an ordinary jump.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Entering DIVING sets a world time dilation factor (default 0.2, configurable) via the game''s time system.
- [ ] Dilation reliably reverts to 1.0 the instant the state leaves DIVING/AIRBORNE (landing, death, or pause/menu), with no stuck slow-mo.
- [ ] Opening the game''s pause menu mid-dive and resuming does not leave dilation stuck active.
- [ ] Verify in-game: trigger the dive, observe the world visibly slow; confirm dilation clears within one frame of landing, and also clears correctly after a mid-dive pause/resume.');

As V, I want my aim turn-speed and weapon fire-rate to stay at normal speed while the world is slowed, so I can place shots precisely instead of fighting slow-motion input.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Camera/aim turn rate is restored to (or exempted from) the global T8 dilation factor while DIVING/AIRBORNE.
- [ ] Weapon fire rate and shoot-input polling are exempted from the dilation; shots fire at normal cadence.
- [ ] Non-exempted systems (enemies, projectiles, environment, V''s own fall arc) remain visibly slowed for contrast — only aim and fire are sped back up.
- [ ] Verify in-game: fire a pistol during the dive; shot cadence matches normal (non-dive) fire rate while the surrounding world is still visibly slow-motion.');

As V, I want the mod to detect the exact moment I hit the ground after a dive and read whether I''m holding a movement input, so the landing can branch correctly.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Mod detects the frame V''s collision transitions from airborne to grounded while in DIVING/AIRBORNE.
- [ ] On that frame, it reads whether a movement input is currently held and stores the flag for the next transition (T11/T12).
- [ ] Grazing a low obstacle mid-dive without ending the airborne arc does not count as a landing (no false positive).
- [ ] Verify in-game: dive and land; the overlay logs exactly one landing event per dive, with the correct held/not-held movement flag in both cases.');

As V, I want to land prone and keep firing from the ground when I land without holding movement, so I can keep shooting from the floor like Max Payne.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Landing with no movement held (T10) transitions AIRBORNE -> PRONE.
- [ ] While PRONE, V can free-aim and fire in any horizontal direction without standing up first.
- [ ] PRONE persists until the player presses a stand/move input (handed to T12''s get-up transition) — not on a timer.
- [ ] Verify in-game: dive, release movement before landing; V ends up prone and can aim/fire 360 degrees from the ground.');

As V, I want to scramble back to my feet when I land holding movement, so the dive flows back into normal play instead of stopping dead.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Landing with movement held (T10) transitions AIRBORNE -> GETUP -> NONE, playing a stand/scramble animation rather than a hard snap to idle.
- [ ] Full normal movement control returns only once GETUP completes.
- [ ] From PRONE (T11), pressing a movement/stand input also runs the same GETUP transition back to NONE.
- [ ] Verify in-game: dive and land while still holding forward — V scrambles up smoothly and regains control; separately, stand up out of PRONE on command and confirm the same transition.');

As V, I want the Shootdodge restricted to pistols, revolvers and small SMGs, so I can''t trigger it while carrying a sniper rifle or a heavy weapon.

## Acceptance

- [ ] T5''s input detection checks the currently equipped weapon''s type before arming the combo.
- [ ] Pistols, revolvers, and small SMGs (explicit allow-list) permit the dive; rifles, shotguns, LMGs, sniper rifles, melee weapons and fists block it.
- [ ] Switching weapons mid-session immediately updates whether the combo is armed — no restart needed.
- [ ] Verify in-game: attempt the combo with a sniper rifle equipped (no trigger), then switch to a pistol and confirm it triggers normally.');

As V, I want camera FOV pull-back, a whoosh cue, and a muffled low-pass on music/ambience during the dive, so the move reads as cinematic rather than a glitch.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Camera FOV pulls back by a configurable amount for the duration of DIVING/AIRBORNE and restores on landing.
- [ ] A whoosh sound effect plays once on dive entry.
- [ ] Music/ambient tracks get a low-pass filter / volume duck while DIVING/AIRBORNE, restored on landing.
- [ ] All three effects are toggleable independently in the debug overlay so each can be verified in isolation.
- [ ] Verify in-game: run a dive -> prone and a dive -> get-up; confirm all three effects start on dive entry and cleanly revert on landing, both paths.');

As V, I want the input combo to launch me into a horizontal dive toward my aim direction, so I leave the ground the way Max Payne does.

## Acceptance

- [ ] A detected T5 combo while in state NONE transitions to DIVING and applies an impulse that sends V airborne, horizontally, toward the camera/aim direction.
- [ ] The initial leap reuses an existing game animation/impulse (a custom .animgraph dive pose is explicitly out of scope here; open question captured in docs/DESIGN.md for a later pass).
- [ ] The dive cannot be re-triggered mid-air: the state guard only allows the transition from NONE.
- [ ] Verify in-game: trigger the combo from standing; V leaves the ground toward the aim direction and the overlay reads DIVING; repeating the combo mid-air does nothing.', '## Story

As V, I want the input combo to launch me into a horizontal leap in the direction I''m moving, locked for the whole dive, so I leave the ground the way Max Payne does.

## Acceptance

