Do:
- **Autoplay toggle** in the toolbar (and a keyboard shortcut), saved in ViewerSettings, restored on start. On: video and audio start playing as soon as they''re shown (today''s behaviour). Off: nothing plays until the user presses play (Space / a play button).
- **Frame preview (video, autoplay off):** instead of a still first frame, the stage cycles through frames taken across the whole video:
  - Skip the ends: start at EdgePercent (default 5%) of the duration and stop at 100% - EdgePercent (95%).
  - Step by StepPercent of the duration (default 10%): frames at 5%, 15%, 25% ... 95%, about 10 frames for the defaults; compute the count from the settings (always include both ends of the window, at least one frame).
  - Show each frame for FrameSeconds (default 1 s), loop; show a small "n / N · mm:ss" marker so the user knows where in the movie each frame is.
  - Pressing play starts real playback (from the start, or from the frame shown if that''s simple; say which in the README).
  - Grab frames without blocking the UI (background, cached per file); a video whose duration can''t be read falls back to the first frame.
- Settings (ViewerSettings + wherever the viewer''s settings are edited): Autoplay (default off? keep the owner''s default: ask nothing, use ON = current behaviour unless the code already has a preference), FramePreviewStepPercent (10), FramePreviewEdgePercent (5), FramePreviewSeconds (1). Clamp to sensible bounds (step 1-50, edge 0-20, seconds 0.2-10).
- Audio with autoplay off: shows its usual view, plays on demand.
- README: document the toggle and the settings.
Verify by build; check with a real clip (R:\MindAttic\Preview\MediaViewer has a format set with 010_clip.mp4) and screenshot the cycling preview.');

Do:
- **Mark in/out** on the video being shown: "Set start" / "Set end" at the current playback position (toolbar buttons plus keys, e.g. I and O), shown on the seek slider as two markers with the kept range highlighted; draggable markers if simple; a "Clear" to reset. Show the kept length (mm:ss.fff).
- **Preview**: play just the kept range (from start marker, stop at end marker).
- **Save** (enabled once a range differs from the whole clip):
  - **Save as new file**: default name `<name>_trim<ext>` beside the original (never overwrite an existing file silently; pick `_trim2` etc.), then select the new file in the viewer.
  - **Overwrite original**: confirm with the library''s themed message box; write to a temp file in the same folder first, then replace the original (send the old one to the Recycle Bin, not a hard delete) only after ffmpeg succeeds.
- **Cut with ffmpeg** (already used by FramePreview; same lookup): default fast lossless stream copy (`-ss` / `-to` with `-c copy`, cuts land on keyframes), and a "Precise (re-encode)" option for frame-accurate cuts; remember the choice in ViewerSettings. Run off the UI thread with progress and a cancel; on failure show ffmpeg''s error and leave the original untouched. No ffmpeg on PATH: disable the feature with a tooltip saying so.
- Same for audio files if it costs nothing extra (same in/out + ffmpeg path); otherwise video only.
- Every new control uses MindAttic.Components themed styles (both themes). README section.
Verify by build; run on a copy of R:\MindAttic\Preview\MediaViewer''s 010_clip.mp4 (never on the owner''s originals), cut both ways, check the outputs play and have the expected length.');

Do:
- **Crop mode** on a still image (toolbar "Crop" button plus key C; Esc leaves the mode): drag a rectangle on the stage; it maps from screen to image pixels correctly at any zoom/pan (Fit and 100%, wheel zoom). Show the selection with a dimmed outside, 8 resize handles, drag inside to move, and a W x H px readout. Optional aspect lock (Free, 1:1, 4:3, 16:9, original) and Shift to constrain; arrow keys nudge.
- **Save** (enabled with a non-empty selection):
  - **Save as new file**: `<name>_crop<ext>` beside the original (never silently overwrite; `_crop2` etc.), then select the new file.
  - **Overwrite original**: confirm with the library''s themed message box; write to a temp file in the same folder, then replace the original only after the write succeeds, sending the old one to the Recycle Bin.
- Keep the format and quality: same encoder as the source (PNG lossless, JPEG at the source''s quality or 95, WebP/AVIF/TIFF/etc. through Magick.NET which the viewer already uses); keep EXIF/ICC metadata and apply EXIF orientation before cropping so the crop matches what''s shown.
- Animated images (GIF/WebP/APNG): crop every frame if Magick.NET makes it simple, otherwise disable crop for animated items with a tooltip.
- Run the encode off the UI thread; on failure show the error and leave the original untouched.
- Every new control uses MindAttic.Components themed styles (both themes). README section.
Verify by build; test only on copies (copy images from R:\MindAttic\Preview\MediaViewer''s format set into your scratchpad), check output dimensions match the selection at Fit and at 100% zoom.');

