## Context

AutoGamePlay (AGP) is the engine-agnostic toolkit that lets an LLM agent (a Claude subagent driving the `agp` CLI) play and playtest first- and third-person PC games: it runs PlayScript (the gameplay scripting language, e.g. `Player.MoveForward(20m).TurnLeft(90)`), executes it with fast reflex controllers while the game is unpaused, pauses the game while the LLM thinks, watches with oracles, keeps frames in a budgeted in-RAM ring buffer, and files deduped bug tickets with evidence. The first consumer is REA.Bloodlines (the s&box port of Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines, epic RB-T245..RB-T272); it must also work for Source 1, GZDoom, and later Unreal (UE4SS), Cyberpunk (CET) and EDuke32. Read docs/DESIGN.md (architecture, decisions), docs/PRIOR_ART.md and docs/ROADMAP.md first; keep the docs current with what you build. No game-specific code in this repo: game specifics live in the game''s own repo as an extension namespace. C#/.NET 10, nullable on, whole-number versions; any in-process LLM call goes through MindAttic.Legion (HOUSE-LAW-4). xUnit tests run against the Fake adapter.');

