Root cause: MainViewModel.Tabs.cs''s `ActiveCliTitles` (M.ORCH-T1424) lists every open Terminals pane''s title, including the Launcher''s own always-open menu pane, in the hover tip''s ''Active CLIs'' line — so a login whose only open tab is its Launcher shows ''Active CLIs: Launcher'' instead of ''Active CLIs: none open''. Fix: exclude Request.IsMenu panes from ActiveCliTitles, matching how Presume()/TeamWall already exclude the Launcher''s menu pane elsewhere.');

**API**
- `ctl:MaCallout.ToolTip=''{Binding Text}''` + `ctl:MaCallout.Placement=''Right''` in place of `ToolTip`: each element gets its own `MaCalloutToolTip`, content kept live; null/empty = no tooltip. The owner''s ToolTipService delays still apply (don''t set ToolTipService.Placement on the owner: WPF lets it win).
- `MaCalloutToolTip : ToolTip` (PreferredSide, read-only Side/ArrowOffset, ArrowSize 7, Gap 2, CornerRadius 4), implicit style in Theme.xaml: MaSurface bubble, MaChromeBorder outline, MaText, MaxWidth 420 wrap; theme brushes only.
- `MaCalloutChrome : Decorator` draws bubble + arrow as one outline.
- `CalloutPlacement.Compute(target, bubble, workArea, preferred, gap, arrowSize, cornerRadius)` is the pure rule set: preferred side if it fits, else opposite, else the roomier; cross-axis shift into the work area; arrow at the target''s centre clamped to cornerRadius + arrowSize from each end.
- Placement runs in Popup''s Custom callback in screen device pixels (WPF passes device-pixel sizes and adds the point to the target''s device top-left), work area from MonitorFromRect/GetMonitorInfo rcWork (SystemParameters.WorkArea fallback), DIP conversion via the target''s per-monitor DPI. Re-placed on every open and on content resize.

**Tests**: 27 new in MaCalloutToolTipTests (placement: fits, flips at right/left/top/bottom, shift up/down/sideways, arrow clamps, short edge, neither fits, target partly off screen, non-zero monitor origin, 150% DPI conversion; chrome layout and outline per side; template brushes; attached props incl. style + binding). Whole suite 271/271.

