For void content (US-T123/T130/T131), pick by `Fields`: ice fields where IceField is high, nebula volumes where Nebula is high, graveyards where Graveyard is high. Tint in-space volumes with the biome''s `Mid`/`Accent` and its dust with `Dust`/`HazeColor` so they match the sky behind them.');

**Contract.** Every embodiable implements IEmbodiable: TakeCharge/HandBack (enter, leave), InputProfile (Helm, Cockpit, Gunner, Station, Satellite, HullWalker, Walker), CameraRig (chase, mount, shoulder), RolePanel (title, state, keys, meter) and Subject (hull, part, point). The switching layer, HUD, picker and co-op read only these. The kind-specific casts in TakeSeat, SeatTarget, SeatScene, SeatKeys, SeatLine, BattleInView, MoveSeatToHost, ManNextGun and the picker are gone.

**Controls.** P embodies the selection or what is under the mouse: a ship''s helm, a hull or station in a fight, or a launched craft. P again releases to the free SpaceGod view. F9 opens the list. '' ; cycle the fight in view. / cycles the hull''s guns. Shift+P puts you on the hull as its next EVA repair worker. Backspace moves up to the host. A role panel on the left lists the held role''s keys.

**Kinds.** Ship helm (any class: fighter, capital, carrier, freighter, and so on), launched craft cockpit, gun mount, station (defence platform or gate fort), satellite, and the new EVA repair worker. Mech (US-T83) and marine (US-T82) are reserved in EmbodimentKind with the Walker profile. Embodiables.WalkersIn is the mech stub and Embodiables.CrewOn is the marine hook.

**Repair worker.** A worker is one of a capital ship''s or station''s damage control teams. W/S and A/D crawl the plating in hull lengths, so it plays the same at either scale. Shift fires the jets. Reach a damaged hardpoint and the worker welds at the team''s own damage-control rate, multiplied by 1.25 for the SpaceGod''s hands. Tapping left mouse in the sweeping zone raises weld quality, up to 2.75x. A miss sputters the torch. While held, the team leaves the AI pool (BattleUnit.EvaHeldTeams, transient and always 0 for AI). AI damage control already repaired, so no baseline was added. HEAD plus the Core change benches 5/5 (digests unchanged).

**Not built.** Station crews do no AI repair in a fight (C# Core parity). Adding it would change the battle digest, so I left it alone. The worker welds on stations at the same team rate.

**Gate (US-T140).** Embodiables.MayEmbody is the single check (always ok). Both SeatAuthority (every peer) and the app''s TakeSeat/TogglePiloting call it and toast the reason. V spawn-and-pilot, Shift+V practice, a save''s resumed helm and FTL/lane re-entry call EnterPiloting directly and bypass it. US-T140 should decide whether those count.

**Who embodies what.** ISessionState.Held / HolderOf(seat) give the lockstep seat state. UnitySpaceApp.EmbodiedNow / EmbodiedBy(unit|ship) add the pilot-loop helm and its co-op holder. Co-op seat key ''W b u team''.

**Global credit (per the design rule).** Law keeps one global `Player` LawRecord (''you'', Law.cpp:85) whose per-faction Standing is shared with EventDirector''s reputation table (playerStanding). Crimes and standing accrue to the player, not to the unit embodied. I left it unchanged.

**Debug.** sg.EvaRepair [game|real] | shots <dir> [quit] goes out on a battleship at a damaged shield generator and screenshots both scales.

**Build.** All of my files compile in UBT. The Core library builds standalone (/W4). Linking the full game was blocked during this session by other agents'' unfinished work (Ftl.inl DeepSpaceEvent, Cheats.cpp Pursuit, Cruise.cpp, Main2.cpp, Comms Pilots.h), so the game was not run.');
- Infinite layer: far star field, galaxies, Milky Way. It never changes.
- Local layer: nebula walls, the surrounding ice or dust field, backdrop giant planets. It''s a finite shell centred on the system at about rim radius and drawn with parallax from the player''s position.
From inside, the local layer looks identical to a skybox. Leaving through the rim, you fly through the thinning wall, with particles streaming past. Looking back, the nebula or field becomes an object enclosing the system and shrinking around its sun. The user is sending an example skybox.');
Plan: use hand-painted spheres like this as hero backdrops alongside the procedural biome skies. Split each one into the two layers: luminance or alpha-key the nebula onto the local parallax shell, and keep the star field as the far layer.
Add credit to docs/ThirdPartyArt.md and the in-game credits.');
- Local layer: a real volumetric nebula (raymarched 3D noise, using the same noise as the procedural sky) inside a finite sphere around the system. It thins as you approach the rim, streams wisps past you, and from outside it reads as a cloud wrapped around the shrinking sun.
- Far layer: hand-painted sky spheres like the Jungle Jim one, plus the procedural star and galaxy panorama.
- Fallback if volumes are too costly: key the painted nebula onto a parallax shell and add fly-through particles.');
- Content: a bright violet, teal and gold nebula with a white-hot core in the centre, dust lanes cut through it, fainter teal and amber filaments wrapping around, and a dense star field. There''s slight stretching at the poles.
- Idea: a ''painted volume''. Project the painting outward into a 3D volume, with density taken from luminance, colour from the texture, and depth jittered with noise. From inside it matches the painting exactly; at the rim it has real depth to thin out through.
- The core is the natural key-light ''heart'' for the light grade.
- Licence: CC BY 4.0, so it can be committed. Credit: Alien Space Nebula 1 (Skybox) by Jungle Jim, CC BY.');

- **Console hook:** `sg.StandDown` sets up the stop. It brings Influence to at least level 4, spawns a pirate band (a corvette and two fighters) closing on a lone freighter near the camera, and puts you at the corvette captain''s helm. The HUD shows a YOUR SQUAD line with the time to contact and "Shift+1 orders them to stand down".
- **Suggested registration** (in StandDownCommand.cpp, as EvaRepairCommand.cpp does): `TourStop::Console("SpaceGod", "stand-down", "Ordering a squad through its leader", "A pirate captain whose band is closing on a lone freighter: order them to stand down; Influence and the captain''s hold decide", "sg.StandDown").Until([](UnitySpaceApp& a, double t){ return a.IsPiloting() && t > 5; }, 30).For(10).AtBothScales()`. A second beat can call `app.OrderSquadStandDown()` to show the answer toast.
- **Influence meter:** it is always on the HUD, top left under the navigator. A stop showing it needs no setup.

The new embody limits matter to the tour. A hull already in a battle cannot be embodied unless the SpaceGod already holds something on that hull, and capitals need Influence 5. A stop that embodies into a fight it did not start from, or takes a capital, must first set `SpaceGodInfluence::Of(world)->Waived = true` (the dev waiver, never saved), as sg.EvaRepair now does.');

