- before: engaged avg **2.6** (runs 2.0-3.5), minimum after the first 30 s **0** in every run; 14.8 of ~31 craft away at their carriers on average; contact 13-16 s.
- after: engaged avg **14.9** (runs 9.5-20.0), minimum after 30 s **1-13** (worst run 1); 2.7 away; contact 7-10 s.
- small craft lost in 300 s 27.7 -> 30.3; capitals'' mean speed 0.07-0.15 km/s before and after (untouched: still slow and heavy).
- In game (sg.BigBattle, game scale, 60 shots a second apart, battle s 26-79): 13-41 engaged each second, 17 strafing at the first shot.

**Changes**
- Rearm: a craft with a working gun stays in the fight once its missiles are gone (bombers still go home for torpedoes, any craft under 40% hull); deck turnaround 30 -> 10 s.
- Carrier craft (interceptor, fighter, heavy, bomber, recon): 1.4x speed and thrust, 1.25x turn and torque, 2.5x hull/shield (1.5x regen), same factors for each so the light/heavy order holds. The plate was needed: kept in the fight at the old plate, 50 craft fell to 14 in a minute (flak made 203 of 265 kills).
- Choreography::Evasion: rolled fire and flak at a small craft lose accuracy with its speed across the gunner''s line, down to 0.4 at 1 km/s; a chaser on its tail is unaffected.
- Targeting: fighters/heavies/bombers count a capital 8 km nearer, crewed interceptors a small craft 5 km nearer; each non-bomber wingman flies its own strafing run on a capital; runs tighter (entry lead 0.6 km + 0.2 length, flip 1 km out).
- War::Spot: fleets open 14 km apart (was 26); station defence platforms keep their old ring.
- Crewed AI fighters'' turn share 0.6 -> 0.8 (player helm tuning untouched).
- sg.BigBattle: pre-roll 50 -> 20 s; its log line adds the engaged count. GameManual "How a fleet action flies" updated.

**Roles**: AI fighters/heavies get the targeting, runs and rearm rule; a craft or hull the player flies picks its own mark (TargetBias 0) and takes aimed fire (Evasion 1 for the player''s hull); the player''s helm tuning is unchanged. Capital/carrier: same speed and turn; carriers relaunch faster. Station: platforms placed as before. Turret, EVA, ejected pilot, free SpaceGod: nothing changes but what they see. Battle km only, so both scales alike.

**Bench**: all five moved legitimately (every scenario fights battles; closer opening; craft specs, rearm, targeting, evasion). From 5e91fde + this (06265cd touches no Core), run twice, identical: sol-idle 0F21C87D858423CD, high-warp 2D5879F3D51DE9D9, economy-year 588B73242252B1CB, battle AAC20E2B824E7237, galaxy-ftl 51047789C2A02F64; HEAD alone matched the old ones. Side effects: the battle scenario (2 battleships + a cruiser a side, no craft) still goes to Sol but runs 3862 ticks not 893; only the opening range touches it, and that fight runs 1100-3600+ s across start dates both before and after (the Bench''s date was a short one before). economy-year: battles started 207 -> 174, total faction treasury +6%, losses 49 -> 57; high-warp +3%, sol-idle and galaxy-ftl +1%.

