**Honest verdict**: much closer to two nests. Strafing-run shots show 8-10 craft with engine trails streaming past a shielded capital at once, and the overviews show two clusters with craft swirling round each. Still short: at overview distance the craft are specks; the dogfight chase shots often frame one craft against empty space; the engaged count sags mid-fight as craft die (one of six probe runs dipped to 1); the system map''s orbit rings clutter some frames (not this ticket).');

**Cause** (reproduced on HEAD in an isolated copy with sg.Comms and a logging probe):
1. Taking a flagship''s helm hands its command to an heir, and War::OwnSpot put that heir 1.5 safe distances *behind* on the old orbit. The helm starts at rest in its frame, so the orbit carried the heir straight into the held hull. The SFS Dauntless started 38.1 km behind and closed at 1.216 km/s, the orbit''s speed. It touched at about 38 s and the Resolute broke up at about 45 s. The next heir, the SFS Aegis, then came on the same way.
2. Fleet::StepAvoidance left held hulls out entirely, so the sidestep was 0.00 km the whole way.

The US-T122 render-sync change (87aa54e) was not involved.

**Fix:**
- The heir of a piloted old flagship takes over *ahead*, so the orbit carries it clear.
- Fleet::ReportHeld: the app reports the flown hull''s real pose and velocity each frame, and StepAvoidance gives every free ship the whole sidestep round it.
- An escort taken out of battle starts at its formation slot, not inside its leader.

All helm takes (P, F9, sg.Comms, spawn-and-pilot) go through EnterPiloting. Roles: capital, heavy, carrier or fighter at a helm get all of it. Station, turret, EVA worker, ejected pilot and free SpaceGod: no change (not flown hulls). Mid-battle: unchanged.

**After the fix:** same scenario (SFS Resolute via sg.Comms). The Dauntless starts 38 km *ahead* and recedes. The Resolute was still flying with its hull at 100% after 150 s. A second seed (ORS Long Night / ORS Umbra) showed the same.

**Bench:** fresh HEAD 0b59812 plus only these hunks. 5 of 5 identical to the 035f46e baselines, no baseline change.

**Still to verify:** the avoidance give-way has not been shown in game. Nothing came near the held hull, and the steering probe could not close on a target. Follow-up: US-T182.

