D:\Projects\MindAttic\MindAttic.Launcher\MindAttic.Launcher\Models\AgentProvider.cs and Services\AgentProviderRegistry.cs model a CLI provider as just {Key, Name, RunCommand} -- a launch-string registry with zero capability-provisioning concept. Services\WindowsTerminalLauncher.cs is presumably where a provider''s RunCommand actually gets invoked to open a terminal tab -- read it first to find the right insertion point.

Scope:
1. Read WindowsTerminalLauncher.cs (and HostAgentCommand.cs / MainMenuCommand.cs, wherever a provider is actually launched) to find where a new CLI session process/tab actually starts.
2. Before that launch, run (or shell out to) mindattic-agent-standard/render-abilities.ps1 and install-hooks.ps1 as a best-effort, idempotent, non-blocking provisioning step: log a warning and continue the launch if either script fails or isn''t found, never block or fail the user''s actual launch over a provisioning hiccup -- this is a live app the user runs daily and must not break.
3. Keep this cheap: both scripts are already idempotent (a no-op rerun is fast), so running them synchronously before each launch should add negligible latency -- but if that proves slow in practice (time it), make it async/fire-and-forget instead and note the tradeoff.
4. Add/update a test in MindAttic.Launcher.Tests covering this (NUnit, matching this project''s existing convention).
5. Read this repo''s own AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md forwarder and any project docs before making changes, and follow its existing code style.
