Checked every place a per-member provider preference could live, per the ticket''s ask: MemberRoster/Member (members table: email, name, role, tier, status, joined/updated -- no provider column), OrgPerson (email, name, aliases, initials -- no provider field), AccountRoster (Claude sign-in rows only), MemberLookup.People(). None of them record or have an obvious slot for a preferred CLI provider. Also checked MindAttic.Launcher''s AgentProviderRegistry/AgentProvider (M.LNCH-T113, the {Key,Name,RunCommand} model this ticket pointed at): its own doc comment says ''There is no persisted default provider anymore -- the interactive menu asks fresh every time a project tab is opened'', i.e. even the app that actually understands multiple providers deliberately does NOT persist a per-person provider preference. So there is no existing, confident source of truth for ''a member''s own configured CLI provider'' anywhere in the codebase -- it would have to be invented from scratch.

Found a second, deeper blocker beyond the missing preference field: StartCommand''s whole --account/OwnLogin mechanism (and the Auto-login picker) is built entirely on AccountDirs (Sessions/AccountDirs.cs), which is Claude-specific by construction -- per-account folders under ~/.claude-accounts, each holding .claude.json, .credentials.json, claude-usage.json, rl-status.json, and signed in via ''claude auth login'' through a BROWSER env var hook. There is no equivalent per-account directory/sign-in abstraction for Codex, Kimi, or Google Antigravity (agy) anywhere in MindAttic.Orchestrator. So even if a members.provider column existed, ''org start <repo> <who>'' would have nowhere to put a Codex/Kimi/agy session ''on that member''s own login'' the way it does for Claude -- those CLIs may not even support isolated multi-account logins the way Claude''s browser SSO does.

Net: this needs two upstream design decisions before it can be built safely, not just a field to add:
(1) Where a member''s preferred provider is recorded -- a new members.provider column (schema migration + orchestrator.sql regen on the live, possibly-concurrently-used SQLite DB), vs. Launcher''s settings.json, vs. somewhere else -- and what it defaults to when absent (must stay Claude for backward compat).
(2) What ''own login'' means at all for Codex/Kimi/agy -- do they need their own AccountDirs-equivalent (per-member config/credential isolation), or does a non-Claude org start just run on the single shared machine-wide login for that CLI (no per-member isolation), which changes the safety story for --account entirely.

Given the user''s explicit instruction to not force through a change I''m not fully confident is safe, and given there''s a real risk of misrouting a real person''s session onto the wrong account/provider, I made no code changes, added no schema fields, and did not touch docs/claude-only-abilities.md (the /research upgrade to TRUE-EQUIVALENT-BUILT should wait for this). Confidence this stays OPEN is high; confidence that forcing a fix now would be safe is low. Recommend the user decide (1) and (2) above, then re-open as implementation work.');
