1. Every per-CLI login that has EVER signed in (has a folder under %USERPROFILE%\.claude-accounts, i.e. every known org member) keeps a permanent root node/tab in the dashboard tree, forever - it never disappears just because it''s currently signed out or has no live CLI (''disconnected''). Ryan decides, by hand, via that node''s own Login/Log out actions, whether it''s actually signed in at any given time; the dashboard doesn''t auto-hide it either way.
2. The ONLY thing that removes a member''s root node from this always-shown set is a new, explicit ''disabled'' status on that member - distinct from merely being disconnected/signed-out. Today MemberRoster.Statuses is only [''active'',''pending'']; this needs a third status (or an equivalent flag) meaning ''skip this one entirely''.
3. For every non-disabled member''s root node, always ensure exactly one ''General Prompt'' CLI is open on that login (the existing WorkspaceRoot/non-repo-specific session type, MainViewModel.Tabs.cs OpenGeneralPromptAsync/StartSessionAsync - already exists, used today from a tab''s right-click ''Open Project > General Prompt''). This needs to become auto-ensured/respawned per login the way Launcher tabs already auto-respawn (see the launcherRespawn/autoOpenLaunchers pattern in MainViewModel.Tabs.cs), not just manually opened.
4. Why: so Ryan can talk directly to that account''s own LLM regardless of project work, AND so that when a login is disconnected, completing its sign-in (the Login right-click action, MainViewModel.LoginCards.cs LoginCommand) happens scoped correctly to that account''s own tab - not accidentally run from an unrelated CLI/window (this is literally what caused the ''This link has already been used'' OAuth error earlier today with Honey''s login attempt, M.ORCH-T1902/1948 investigation).');

Full confirmed spec (1,3,4 confirmed as originally stated; 2 replaced by the above):
1. Every per-CLI login that''s ever signed in keeps a permanent root node in the tree forever, regardless of current connect state.
2. A root node''s state is Connected / Disconnected / Disabled (tri-state), Disabled being an explicit manual action distinct from Disconnected.
3. Every Connected or Disconnected (i.e. non-Disabled) node always has exactly one ''General Prompt'' CLI auto-ensured/respawned on it (same pattern as Launcher tab auto-respawn), so Ryan can talk to that account''s LLM directly and so sign-in for a Disconnected node happens scoped to its own tab, not some unrelated window.
4. A true Delete action removes a node from both the tree and the member list (distinct from Disabled), likely via the existing ''orchestrator members remove <email>'' plus removing the tree node; default to NOT deleting the underlying .claude-accounts folder/credentials unless Ryan separately asks for that.');
