2. Accept each invite and sign each login in as ITSELF, never as Ryan: in the Orchestrator dashboard open the login''s own tree node (Honey, Waffle) and use its sign-in, or run `orchestrator org login honey` / `orchestrator org login waffle` (same as orchestrator login --account <email>). It opens the browser: copy the URL into a private/incognito window where Ryan is NOT signed in to claude.ai, sign in as honey@ / waffle@ (mailbox code), approve. A normal window signs it in as Ryan (the M.ORCH-T1896 bug: Honey''s folder showed Ryan''s usage). Confirm `orchestrator members` shows "yes (own login)" and not "borrowed from".
3. Clear MemberUntil for them (it currently hides their tabs from 2026-11-11) or set it to the day before renewal; let them run their tokens out (Ryan said about 10 days from 2026-11-22, i.e. about 2026-12-02).
4. Before the renewal date: Settings > Organization > Members > remove both, AND lower Total seats (Organization settings > Organization and access > Manage). Removing a member alone does not lower the bill; the seat reduction takes effect at the next renewal and can be submitted early.
5. Then `orchestrator members remove honey@mindattic.com` / waffle@ if listed, and set MemberUntil to now.

Orchestrator help: `orchestrator remind` is one-shot only (--at, --to, --list, --cancel); there is no --every or --until-ticket, and `members set --status` only changes the local roster, not Anthropic seats. So 10 one-shot reminders (daily 9:00, 2026-11-23 to 2026-12-02) were added, texted to the owner via Psst; list them with `orchestrator remind --list`. Re-add or cancel them once the renewal date is known. Ticket stays OPEN until the owner confirms steps 1-5 are done.');

