- GameAudio.h/.cpp: public enum class Placement { Panned, Headphones, Mono }; static void SetPlacement(Placement); a Place(FSoundAttenuationSettings&, float minCm) helper called from Attenuation() before an attenuation is cached. Place: Mono turns bSpatialize off; Headphones sets NonSpatializedRadiusStart = the sound''s min distance, NonSpatializedRadiusEnd = 0, mode OmniDirectional (narrows near sounds); Panned leaves engine defaults (Auto unchanged). SetPlacement re-applies Place to every cached attenuation (min distance cm = key >> 32) and calls AdjustAttenuation(c->AttenuationSettings->Attenuation) on every live voice.
- AudioOutput.h/.cpp: SpeakerMode() declares audio.speakerMode (Auto, Headphones, Stereo speakers, Mono, Surround 5.1, Surround 7.1; default Auto), registered from Declare(). Applying stores the mode and, only when Active() (skips scripted runs), calls GameAudio::SetPlacement. Query() also reads FMixerDevice::GetNumDeviceChannels() on the audio thread; while a Surround mode is chosen Tick re-checks every 2 s. Describe() sets the row description to "Windows reports stereo: set 5.1 / 7.1 in Windows Sound settings." when the device has fewer channels than the chosen Surround mode; guard with a speakersBuilt flag (Applying runs while the static setting is being built).
- Include rule: since US-T661 (9a3a666) both .cpp include their own header first, then Audio/AudioMixerIncludes.h.
- Known gap (split it, don''t do it here): on a 5.1/7.1 device, Stereo/Headphones aren''t folded to 2 channels; UE 5.8 has no channel-count override, it needs a custom submix effect.');
