RECOMMEND: Universal Sound FX (Imphenzia), https://assetstore.unity.com/packages/audio/sound-fx/universal-sound-fx-17256
- $24.97 on the 50% sale (list $49.95), v1.6 (2025-02-28), 1.4 GB, 1,072 ratings. Sale prices come and go; if it is back at $49.95 it is still the best value.
- Licence: Standard Unity Asset Store EULA, Extension Asset, Single Entity (individuals/small business). Royalty-free in commercial games incl. mobile; just not resellable as a sound library. Covers our Android/iOS/WebGL builds.
- Strengths: UI, pickups, power-ups, magic/casts, whooshes, impacts, 8-bit/sci-fi, voice. Matches ~all 66 current cue files'' families: ui.* (10), battle.cast/channel/orb/powerup/pickup/whoosh/turn/victory/defeat/heal/miss/slide/dash/crit/clang/explosion/glass/shatter, element.* (7), status.*, camp.*, story.quest.* (about 45 of 52 groups, roughly 85%). Gaps: weapon-specific hits (sword/axe/bow/claw), per-family death cries, terrain footsteps, shell crack, egg squelch, slime squelch/vomit, steam-train whistle. Those stay on make_sfx.py cues or get a small second pack later.

ALTERNATIVES (all Gravity Sound, same EULA, neither has enough ratings to judge):
- RPG Sound Effects Bundle, $109.99, 1,332 sounds, v1.0 2022, no sale. Would cover swords/monsters better but 4x the price, unrated. https://marketplace.unity.com/packages/audio/sound-fx/rpg-sound-effects-bundle-237713
- Medieval Fantasy RPG Sound Effects, $39.99, 406 sounds, v1.0 2020, 57 MB, unrated. https://marketplace.unity.com/packages/audio/sound-fx/foley/medieval-fantasy-rpg-sound-effects-180203
Not chosen: Big Fantasy Sound Effects Bundle ($299, 4,792 sounds) is overkill.
Because the ticket says "single source", Universal Sound FX is the safer, well-reviewed one; its melee/creature gap is the only reason to consider the $109.99 bundle instead.

OWNER STEPS (about 10 min)
1. Open the Asset Store link above, sign in with the Unity ID the project uses.
2. Choose license "Single Entity", Add to cart, check out (tax added), pay.
3. In Unity: Window > Package Manager > My Assets > Universal Sound FX > Download (1.4 GB; do not Import into the project).
4. Optional audition first: the page''s Audio preview plays samples; listen for sword hit and death-cry equivalents. Unity refund policy applies if it fails.
