- SessionStep.Reflection (string?): the fixed reflection question in the attempt''s exam language. Set only on an ended step (State=Ended) when the examiner ended the exam (EndReason EvidenceComplete, TurnLimit or TimeUp) and the student has not yet answered or skipped it. CurrentAsync keeps returning it until then, so a reload comes back to it. Null after Abandoned (student finished early or staff ended it) and for sessions ended before this change.
- SessionOrchestrator.AnswerReflectionAsync(org, sessionId, studentUserId, string? text, string mode, ct): mode voice, or text (typed-answer accommodation). Text is trimmed; empty counts as skipped; over ClosingReflection.MaxLength (20,000) is refused. Returns the ended step with Reflection null.
- SessionOrchestrator.SkipReflectionAsync(org, sessionId, studentUserId, ct).
- Both are idempotent: with nothing waiting (already answered or skipped, never offered, or exam still running) they change nothing and return the current step.
- Hub: AnswerReflection(sessionId, text, mode = voice) (typed text needs the accommodation, like Answer) and SkipReflection(sessionId).
- Wording: ClosingReflection.English / Spanish / Korean, ClosingReflection.Prompt(language). English is the ticket''s suggestion; es and ko are my translations for the owner to confirm.
