```powershell
cd D:\Projects\MindAttic\GridGame.Unity
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force D:\Secrets | Out-Null
& "C:\Program Files\Unity\Hub\Editor\6000.4.3f1\Editor\Data\PlaybackEngines\AndroidPlayer\OpenJDK\bin\keytool.exe" -genkeypair -v -keystore D:\Secrets\gridgame-upload.jks -alias upload -keyalg RSA -keysize 4096 -validity 10000
notepad android-signing.env
```

keytool asks for a **keystore password** (twice), then name, organisational unit, organisation (MindAttic), city, state, two-letter country code, then `yes`; press Enter at the key password to reuse the keystore password.

In notepad paste this, put your password in, save, close:

```
GG_ANDROID_KEYSTORE=D:\Secrets\gridgame-upload.jks
GG_ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASS=<the keystore password>
GG_ANDROID_KEY_ALIAS=upload
```

Then save `D:\Secrets\gridgame-upload.jks` and the password in your password manager (as a file attachment).

## Done when
In the same PowerShell, `git status --short android-signing.env` prints nothing (git ignores it) and `Test-Path D:\Secrets\gridgame-upload.jks` prints True. Reply ''keystore done''; never paste the password.', '2026-11-27T09:33:14Z');

