Owner 2026-11-03: "these new coordinates and zoom are kept in memory in the character''s Thumbnail properties; it always uses the real existing portrait and simply zooms in and offsets; that way the portrait is always in memory and when the enemy dies you can just spawn a portrait of the actual full portrait to shake and die; no duplicating assets."

**Shape** (`ClassDef.Thumbnail`, `Core/Content/ContentModels.cs`, pure C#):
```json
"Thumbnail": { "Zoom": 2.4, "X": 0.52, "Y": 0.21 }
```
- `X`, `Y`: the portrait point (fractions of the portrait''s width / height, top-left origin) that sits at the thumbnail''s centre.
- `Zoom`: portrait width ÷ thumbnail side (1 = the whole portrait width fills the square). Aspect is always kept.
- Resolution-independent, so it holds for every thumb size (board token, timeline icon, menu cards).
- Distinct from `Crop` (the cut-in bust''s eye framing), which is unchanged.

**Acceptance**
- `ContentLoader.Validate` rejects a Thumbnail with Zoom outside [0.25, 20] or X/Y outside [-0.5, 1.5].
- One-shot `tools/migrate_thumbnails.py` writes a Thumbnail for every class into `classes.json` that reproduces today''s `Resources/Thumbs/<id>.png` framing: the box `import_art.py` cut from the GridGame2026 source (override, face or figure crop) mapped through the alpha-bbox trim into `Resources/Portraits/<id>.png` space. Minimal JSON diff (only the new blocks).
- `import_art.py` stops writing `Thumbs/` and stops owning crop overrides (the Thumbnail is the override).
- BIBLE records the property and the owner''s rule.', '2026-11-03T18:23:08Z');

**Acceptance**
- One helper (e.g. `Ui.PortraitThumb(host, classId)`) draws a portrait child inside an `overflow: hidden` host using percentages only (width = Zoom×100%, height = Zoom×aspect×100%, left = 50% − X×width, top = 50% − Y×height), so it is right at any size without layout passes.
- Used by: board tokens (`UnitView.Art`, corpses use their `CorpseOf` class), `Ui.Thumb` (all hub/menu/bestiary/party cards), the dialogue faces (`DialogueScreen` — `Art.Exists("Thumbs/…")` checks become a portrait-exists check), the battle status row, and the timeline turn icons (circle mask; the icon now uses the thumbnail framing for heroes and enemies alike instead of the enemy `Pixel/` sprite or a pre-cut thumb).
- `Art.Thumb` and `Assets/Gaiden/Resources/Thumbs/` (png + meta) are deleted; `Art.Portrait` textures are the only unit art loaded.
- Death and other full-portrait moments keep using the same in-memory `Art.Portrait` texture.
- Verified by play: `tools/build.ps1`, harness smoke + sweep screenshots looked at (board, timeline, party, bestiary, dialogue), plus a MindAttic.Capture recording of a battle.', '2026-11-03T18:23:10Z');

Owner 2026-11-03: "a special standalone application which allows me to load a portrait, and determine its thumbnail through zooming and targeting the square you need to cut out, then that cut out needs to be converted to timeline icons … make sure that this tool is separate … so each unit is exactly what I want them to look like and at what zoom and offset."

**Where.** `tools/ThumbnailStudio/` — its own .NET 10 WPF project and exe, outside `Assets/` (Unity never sees it). Reads `Assets/Gaiden/Resources/Content/classes.json` and `Assets/Gaiden/Resources/Portraits/<id>.png`.

