Root cause (confirmed from AbilityUsageSoak battle records, GAIDEN_ABILITY_PARTY=campaign, d10, after the wave-3 trim): roughly 35-50% of every hero action in these runs is a forced Guard (one record: 133 of 272 total turns = 49%; a Victory record: 169 of 354 = 48%). The GG-T311 ActionFits/MinActionSeconds gate refuses an action that does not fit before the next enemy turn, forcing Guard instead; with only 3 heroes to interleave actions among (vs the 5-6 used in the general soak baseline), far fewer of the party''s turns find a fitting window, and the party spends roughly half the battle Guarding instead of acting, even though Rally (forced-Guard stacking, up to RallyMaxStacks=5) is meant to offset exactly this by slowing enemies.

This intersects two of GG-T311''s own open owner questions (recorded in .agent/RECOVERY.md''s history): whether to keep Rally as the deadlock-breaker, and whether the ~2.4s enemy bar-crossing at difficulty 10 is too frantic. It also means the very first battle of a new game, at the default/designed difficulty, is only winnable a handful of times in 16 even by the skilled bot.

Needs a deliberate balance pass (likely scaling MinActionSeconds/RallyMaxStacks/EnemySpeed by live party size, or owner direction on which lever to pull), not a quick stage-content trim -- that''s why this wasn''t fixed directly under GG-T313, which was scoped to verification plus small content-only tuning. GG-T313''s stages.json trim (one fewer frog in Green Valley I wave 3) is committed and stays; this ticket is the deeper mechanic-level follow-up.', '2026-11-07T03:11:49Z');
