Cause: Tests/Core.Tests/AbilityUsageSoak.cs''s per-stage soak path (the one polish.py''s run_soak drives) always fields a flat five-hero rotating party for every stage (plan.Add((Enumerable.Range(0,5)...)) unless GAIDEN_ABILITY_PARTY=campaign is set, which polish.py never sets. BattleEngine.PartyScale (BattleConfig.cs, GG-T321, landed 2026-11-07) scales enemy HP and strike by 1 + EnemyScalePerExtraHero(0.3) * max(0, PartySize - PartyScaleBaseHeroes(3)). A flat five-hero party is +2 over the baseline of 3, so every soak battle fights enemies at 1.6x the HP and damage they are designed against (BattleConfig.cs''s own comment: ''the starting three fights foes as designed''). AbilityUsageSoak.CampaignPartySize(c, stage) already computes the campaign-correct roster size per stage (3 at greenvalley-01, growing as story-beat joins land) -- it is used only on the GAIDEN_ABILITY_PARTY=campaign path, which polish.py''s run_soak does not set.

Timing: GG-T321 (party-size scaling) landed 2026-11-07, after the 2026-11-05 measurement that had Tithe Moors I (greenvalley-01) at 75% casual win / 59% HP-left (BIBLE Sec 22.4/22.7). The 2026-11-17 pass (GG-T215/GG-T276) now measures greenvalley-01 at 12% (1/8, GAIDEN_ABILITY_STAGE scoped sample). The 60% enemy buff from a mismatched party size, landing in between, is the leading suspect for that collapse, well beyond the three stages originally flagged.

Fix options (needs an owner/design call, not a blind tuning pass): (1) have polish.py''s run_soak pass GAIDEN_ABILITY_PARTY=campaign so POL-G1/G2/G6 measure the party size each stage is actually designed against; changes the POL-G baseline for every past measurement in docs/polish/baseline.json, so wants a deliberate re-baseline. (2) Keep the flat-five soak as an intentional ''worst case, max roster'' stress test, and re-derive the POL-G1/G2 win-rate bands for that assumption instead of the designed-for-three assumption. (3) Lower EnemyScalePerExtraHero or raise PartyScaleBaseHeroes so a 5-hero early-game party is not 60% harder than a 3-hero one -- but this is also a core difficulty-identity knob (GG-T321, ''difficulty 10 gets its challenge from party size''), not a stray tuning number, so changing it needs the same sign-off as (1)/(2).

Test: re-run python tools/polish.py --no-player --balance with option (1)''s change (GAIDEN_ABILITY_PARTY=campaign added to run_soak''s casual/greedy env dicts) and confirm POL-G1 moves toward the 55-85% band broadly, not just on greenvalley/lanternroad/cave.', '2026-11-18T03:48:24Z');

