Findings from a first pass (2026-11-25, no code written; start from here, don''t re-read everything):
- Wave opening: OpenPartyWindow() in Core/Battle/BattleRunner.Setup.cs (~line 304) schedules only foe icons with an OpeningWindowSeconds (3 s) hold; in HeroTimeline also schedule hero icons inside that hold so heroes open each wave first.
- Mid-battle foes: SpawnEnemy (~line 419); tamed units in BattleRunner.Tame.cs (~line 57).
- Entry by Speed: BattleEngine.EntrySeconds(Unit) uses Formulas.ReferenceEnemySpeed(level); add a hero reference speed (BattleConfig constant or Formulas).
- Arrival loop: Tick() in Core/Battle/BattleRunner.Timeline.cs (~lines 103-146) treats every non-independent turn icon as RunEnemyTurn. Hero icons need their own branch: reset, then ScheduleReentry with RecoverBaseSeconds. Handing control to the player on arrival is GG-T808.
- Spacing: ScheduleReentry skips non-enemy icons; record that TimelineSpacing does not space hero icons.
- Tie rule to record in BIBLE 2.4: today casts > hazards > turns > lower entry id (Earlier/ArrivalRank); proposal: a hero turn beats a foe turn on the same tick.
- Tests: TurnRules.Require throws for HeroTimeline until GG-T808 and BattleRunner is internal, so the race/replay tests need a small public clock-advance hook (or wait for GG-T808); the ''faster hero enters further left'' test only needs BattleEngine.Create plus BarU/TicksUntilTurn.', '2026-11-25T15:42:06Z');

