Why: since IP-T515 the study only runs inside the Hub (`idiotproof research gappers explore ...`), and the installed Hub at C:\Apps\IdiotProof predates this commit. Agents may not publish or redeploy the Hub, so the new commands are not callable until the owner publishes.

What remains, in order (outside 04:00-09:30 ET; the commands also pause themselves 03:55-09:35 ET on weekdays; the Azure research DB is awake 03:30-20:30 ET):
1. Owner publishes the Hub (tools\publish-all.ps1), when no live-money risk.
2. `idiotproof research gappers explore --command auctions-pull` (train Tier20/50/100 gapper days + matched controls; ~1 request per train day per 100 symbols, a few hundred to ~1.5k requests; files in D:\IdiotProofData\gapper-study\auctions\yyyy\; resumable).
3. `idiotproof research gappers explore --command auctions` (report: official cross vs 09:30 bar open / 15:59 close, cross size, cross vs PM high) -> runs/explore/auctions-*.md.
4. `idiotproof research gappers explore --command quotes-pull` (needs the 08:30 explore panel cache; NBBO +-60 s of each simulated entry/exit of the 08:30 buy-now pool; 2 requests per trade at the 200 rpm gate; D:\IdiotProofData\gapper-study\quotes\entries-0830-buy-now.csv; resumable).
5. `idiotproof research gappers explore --command quotes-check` -> runs/explore/quotes-check-*.md. Then close with the report commit.

Note: no explore configuration cleared the finalist bar (A04 is detection only), so the quotes use the pool any entries finalist would have come from, not a finalist. Train only; holdout untouched.', '2026-11-19T08:47:54Z');

