`{Universe}/{BookCode}` export folder holds only the newest bundle, with every prior version
moved to a **sibling** `Archives` tree (`ePub/MindAttic/Archives/{Universe}/{BookCode}/v<N>/`)
instead of nesting `Archives\v<N>` directly under the live bundle folder.

`ExportArchive` (Paths/ExportArchive.cs) currently hardcodes the nested shape: `Clean` and
`ArchiveCurrent` always write into `<nodeDir>\Archives\v<N>`, and `CurrentVersion` always reads
from there. Prose''s `ExportCleanupService` is the only consumer of these two methods, so the fix
is to stop the library from deciding WHERE the archive tree lives, and let the caller pass that
in explicitly — the library should only know HOW to archive a version once the location is given.

Change:
- `Clean(string nodeDir, int? fallbackVersion = null)` -> `Clean(string nodeDir, string archiveDir, int? fallbackVersion = null)`
- `ArchiveCurrent(string nodeDir, int version)` -> `ArchiveCurrent(string nodeDir, string archiveDir, int version)`
- `CurrentVersion(string nodeDir)` -> `CurrentVersion(string nodeDir, string archiveDir)`
- Each method''s body: replace every `Path.Combine(nodeDir, ArchivesFolder, ...)` with
  `Path.Combine(archiveDir, ...)` (the "v<N>" folder is still appended inside the method). Nothing
  else about the copy/stamp/cover-stays logic changes.
- `ArchivesFolder` constant stays (ArtifactWriter.ArchiveExisting still uses it for a different,
  single-file archiving feature — do not touch that method).
- `ManuscriptExporter.ExportBundleAsync` (the library''s own internal caller, currently unused by
  any consumer in the workspace — grepped, zero call sites) must keep its EXACT prior behavior:
  pass `Path.Combine(request.Directory, ExportArchive.ArchivesFolder)` as the new `archiveDir`
  argument at its three call sites (CurrentVersion, Clean, ArchiveCurrent), so its own nested
  shape is unchanged.
- Update `MindAttic.Export.Tests/Paths/ExportArchiveTests.cs`: every call site needs the new
  `archiveDir` argument. Use a second temp subfolder (sibling of the existing `Dir`, e.g.
  `Path.Combine(Temp.Path, "..", "Archives")` or a second `TempDirTestBase`-provided dir) as
  `archiveDir` in place of the old `Path.Combine(Dir, "Archives")`, and update the `Archived(v)`
  helper to read from `archiveDir\v<N>` instead of `Dir\Archives\v<N>`. Keep every existing
  assertion''s intent (what moves where, stamping on collision, cover.jpg staying live, "never
  deletes" full-cycle test) — only the literal path changes.
- Bump `MindAttic.Export.csproj` `<Version>` to the next whole number (HOUSE-LAW-1) — 6.0.0.
- `dotnet build` + `dotnet test` green, then `dotnet pack`, then copy the new
  `MindAttic.Export.6.0.0.nupkg` into `C:\LocalNuGet` AND into `D:\Projects\MindAttic\Prose\lib\local-packages\`
  (Prose''s NuGet.config local feed) so Prose can pick it up once its own `Prose.Core.csproj`
  PackageReference is bumped to 6.0.0 (that bump happens on the Prose side, tracked under
  PRS-T942 — don''t touch Prose''s repo from here).

This is a pure refactor — no behavior change for any existing caller until Prose''s own
`ExportCleanupService` (separate ticket, Prose repo) starts passing a sibling-tree `archiveDir`
instead of the old nested one.', '2026-11-17T02:23:55Z');

