Cause: AccountScope.IsSignedIn (Services/AccountScope.cs) only checks .claude.json''s oauthAccount.emailAddress. The API-key login (MindAttic.Orchestrator.Core''s ApiKeyPerson) never gets an oauthAccount — ApiKeyPerson.EnsureConfig only sets hasCompletedOnboarding and approves the Vault key in customApiKeyResponses.approved. So AccountScope.Ensure always thinks it''s never signed in and runs ''orchestrator login --account'', which drives a real claude.ai OAuth sign-in for an email that was never meant to have a claude.ai account.

Fix: AccountScope (or AccountScope.Ensure) needs to special-case api-key@mindattic.vault: treat it as ''signed in'' when its .claude.json has the Vault key''s tail approved in customApiKeyResponses.approved (ClaudeKeyChoice''s format in MindAttic.Orchestrator.Core), not when there''s an oauthAccount. Never run the claude.ai OAuth flow for this login; preparing its folder is MindAttic.Orchestrator.Core''s ApiKeyPerson.Prepare, which the Orchestrator''s own OpenLauncherPaneAsync already calls before opening its Launcher pane (MainViewModel.Tabs.cs) -- this path (MindAttic.Launcher launched standalone with --account api-key@mindattic.vault, not through the Orchestrator''s Open Launcher) is the one that skips it.', '2026-10-27T02:58:48Z');

Cause: settings.json (%APPDATA%\MindAttic\MindAttic.Launcher\settings.json) contains 6 byte-for-byte identical Project entries for RogueTrader.Overwatch and 6 for RogueTrader.Shared. Nothing in the pipeline (ProjectRoster.Sorted, WorkspaceCommitter, ProjectTree.Level) dedupes the roster -- every duplicate record is faithfully iterated/displayed. ProjectTree''s group-then-expand logic at Services/ProjectTree.cs is intentionally designed to let two distinct projects that share a full name both surface as separate leaves (see ProjectTreeTests.cs), so true duplicate records just fan out 1:1 through it. No currently-reachable code path reintroduces the dupes (ProjectDiscovery.FindUnregistered already guards against re-adding known paths); this looks like historical data corruption, e.g. an older pre-guard version of DiscoverProjectsMenu.AddOne running more than once, or a bad settings merge/restore.

Fix: (1) remove the 5 redundant copies each of RogueTrader.Overwatch and RogueTrader.Shared from settings.json, keeping one of each; (2) add DistinctBy((Name, Path)) dedup in ProjectRoster.Sorted (Services/ProjectRoster.cs) as defense-in-depth so corrupted/duplicated roster data can never fan out into every consumer again.

Test: unit test on ProjectRoster.Sorted asserting duplicate (Name, Path) entries collapse to one.

