## Story
As the owner, I open a **Collection** in MindAttic.Media.Viewer and cycle through every item in it with the arrow keys,
whatever its source. A Collection is any gathering of media:
- the contents of one folder;
- a folder and all its nested folders (recursive);
- several sibling folders;
- any hand-picked list of 1..M files drawn from 1..M folders (mixed).

## Acceptance
- One Collection model (an ordered list of sources: file | folder | folder-recursive), resolved to an ordered item list,
  filtered to supported media; duplicates removed; stable, predictable order (by source, then natural name sort).
- Ways to open one: command line (several paths and/or a `--recursive` flag), dropping several files/folders on the window,
  a saved collection file (e.g. `.macollection` JSON listing the sources) that can be reopened, and a Capture preview set
  opening as a Collection (MindAttic.Capture `capture set` output).
- The viewer shows where the current item lives (folder) and its position in the collection (n / total).
- Picks up files added to watched source folders while open (so a preview set filling up during headless work shows new
  items), without losing the current position.
- Check how Capture preview sets are opened today (R:\MindAttic\Preview, /preview skill) and make that the same path.', '2026-11-26T15:26:59Z');

