this login''s subagent-slot load, i.e. Subagents (how many are running now) over
SubagentAllowance (how many may run at once right now), e.g. "2 of 6" -> 33%. Both numbers
are already computed server-side (Pacer.cs''s Pace record) and already flow per-tab through
MainViewModel.Pace (Phases.cs:162, snapshot?.Pace, scoped per login by LoginScope.For) -- no
new plumbing needed, this is a pure view-layer addition.

Design:
- New `LambdaOf(Pace? pace)` alongside `TabUsagePairsOf` in MainViewModel.TabStatus.cs:
  null SubagentAllowance -> hidden (unpaced, same as today''s other figures); SubagentAllowance
  == 0 -> 100% (a hard stop means no room for a new one, regardless of how many still happen
  to be running); otherwise 100 * Subagents / SubagentAllowance, uncapped (so e.g. 6 running
  against a since-lowered allowance of 5 correctly reads 120%, matching how the 5hr/week
  figures already read past 100% at their cutoff).
- Extend `TabUsagePairsOf` to append " | λ: Z%" when present, so it flows automatically into
  TabTrailing (the on-tab text) and TabTip/TabHoverTip (the tooltip) exactly like the existing
  two figures, no separate wiring.
- No width handling needed: confirmed the person tab''s width is already computed from its
  own content (MainWindow.xaml.cs''s SizePersonTabs/NaturalWidth, M.ORCH-T1096) rather than a
  fixed size, re-measuring whenever the trailing text''s size changes, so the tab simply grows
  to fit the third figure. (The code comment at MainViewModel.TabStatus.cs:93 claiming "the tab
  is a fixed 230 wide" is stale since T1096 superseded it -- worth a one-line fix alongside
  this ticket.)', '2026-10-27T22:58:53Z');

