- TermSession.cs: pi.hProcess was never CloseHandle''d (leaked every session) -- closed in WatchExit alongside hThread.
- TermSession.cs: ptyIn/ptyOut FileStreams never disposed when CreateProcessW failed after CreatePseudoConsole succeeded -- now disposed in that failure path.
- RelayConnection.cs WriteInput: HasLink()-then-Send() was a TOCTOU that could drop a keystroke with no InputDropped event if the link dropped in between -- Send() now does the check-and-enqueue atomically under one lock and WriteInput raises InputDropped whenever it returns false; new regression test.
- TermBridge.cs/GatewayApp.cs: socket.Abort() had no try/catch, so a throw there orphaned the detach-audit write and a background watch task -- wrapped in a TryAbort helper.
- TermGatewayTokens.cs: the corrupt-key-file repair path was missing the concurrent-winner re-check its sibling branch has -- now re-reads and adopts whichever key actually won the race.
- TermBus.cs: the sends dictionary grew forever (one entry per killed hosted session, never removed) -- now swept on a 30s idle timeout via ConcurrentDictionary''s conditional remove.
- GatewayCertificates.cs FromStore: rejected certificate candidates were never disposed -- now disposed.
- Registration.cs End(): a timed-out worker-thread join still unconditionally deleted the registry file, which the worker''s still-in-flight write could then recreate -- now only deletes on a successful join.
- RelayTerminal.cs: SuppressResize was reset synchronously right after firing an un-awaited ResizeAsync, making the suppression window ~0 -- now properly awaits the resize first.
- RelayConnection.cs/ViewerWindow.cs: two CancellationTokenSources (sending, stop) were Cancel()''d but never Disposed -- now disposed.
- GatewayBroadcast.cs: the seen tuple was read/written from a Timer callback without a lock -- added a narrow pollGate lock.

Held off (needs human input, not fixed): ViewerWindow.cs EndCli''s confirm-dialog can be force-closed by the owning window closing mid-prompt, silently never killing the CLI -- the correct behavior (force-kill anyway vs. cancel the close vs. something else) is a product decision. Also held off: ViewerWindow.cs''s ReconnectingChanged isn''t wired up like its sibling RemoteViewerWindow (feature-parity gap, not a defect) -- would need to interact with the existing ShowNotSent save/restore mechanism, not a trivial change.

