`MainWindow.xaml:164`, bound to `OrgTabs`) to show an attention marker when that login''s work has
finished since I last looked at that tab, so I don''t have to keep clicking through tabs that are
already done.

**Current state:** The tab header (`MainWindow.xaml:198-227`) already shows mutually-exclusive
status badges from `MainViewModel.TabStatus.cs` -- idle ("zzz"), busy (spinner), asking ("?", blocked
on you) and disabled (lock). None of them mean "finished and you haven''t looked yet" -- that state
doesn''t exist today. Ticket closure is tracked (`FinishedViewModel`/`plan.Finished`) but only shown
on the global tab, not per login; tab selection exists (`MainViewModel.Tabs.cs` `Select`/
`SelectedTabChanged`) but nothing timestamps when a tab was last viewed.

**Design:**
- New per-tab badge state, e.g. `HasUnseenCompletion`, computed and refreshed the same way the
  existing badges are (`RaiseTabStatus()`, `MainViewModel.TabStatus.cs:418-427`).
- "Completed" = a ticket closes that''s attributed to that login (via `TicketAttribution`/
  `AgentBoardRow.OwnLogin`), not just the workspace-wide finished list.
- "Viewed" = the user selects that tab. Each tab keeps an in-memory "last viewed" timestamp,
  compared against the login''s latest completion timestamp.
- Badge clears the instant the tab is selected; no persistence across app restarts for v1.
- Badge only shows when the tab is *not* currently selected and *not* already showing busy/asking
  (still-working or blocked-on-you outrank "something finished earlier").

**Acceptance criteria:**
- Closing a ticket attributed to a login lights up that login''s tab with the new badge, unless that
  tab is the one currently selected.
- Selecting the tab clears the badge immediately.
- Badge never appears alongside Busy or Asking; may appear alongside Idle.
- Unit-tested at the view-model level (badge computation), not a full UI test.

**Open questions for approval:**
1. In-memory-only "last viewed" (resets on app restart) OK for v1, or does it need to persist?
2. Any preferred glyph/color, or is "!" in an accent color (distinct from the existing "?" asking
   badge) fine?', '2026-10-29T18:10:53Z');

