Ryan''s person tab showed the gray "zzz" idle badge while his Unity.GridGame CLI (pid 72216, session 75baad4a) was working with 12 subagents and 12 /allocate claims.

![image 1](file:///D:/Projects/MindAttic/MindAttic.Tickets/data/attachments/_inbox/75baad4a-64c9-4da9-b1f8-72f0ae88d93a/2026-11-02-image-1.png)

## Cause

The snapshot is correct. `status-snapshot.json`, 25s old, has:
- `GlobalEmail = ryandebraal@mindattic.com`.
- This session in `OwnLogins` as `ryandebraal@mindattic.com`, because the CLI runs on the per-CLI folder `~/.claude-accounts/ryandebraal@mindattic.com`.
- Its agent row: State=Working, Subagents=12, Claims=12, OwnLogin=`ryandebraal@mindattic.com`.

The bug: a CLI on a per-CLI login whose email equals the global login''s email ends up on no tab.
- `LoginScope.Tabs` suppresses that email''s own tab ("the global login''s own account gets no second tab", the `e != globalEmail` filter). Its member, Ryan, is shown only by the global tab (Email null).
- `LoginScope.For(all, null)` calls `Keep(login => Same(login, null))`, which keeps only sessions, hosts and agents whose OwnLogin is null. So the agent with OwnLogin == GlobalEmail is dropped.
- Result: `MainViewModel.AnyAgentWorkingOf(snapshot.Agents)`, `WorkingCount` and `HostCount` all see nothing for this CLI, and `ActivityOf` returns Idle.

## Fix

In `LoginScope.For`, when `email` is null, keep logins that are null OR equal (normalized, `AccountDirs.Normalize`) to `all.GlobalEmail`. That covers the sessions, Launcher tabs (`h.OwnLogin`) and agents `Keep` filters. Check `LoginBoard` and `OrgScope` for the same null-only match.

## Test

In `LoginScopeTests`, take a snapshot whose GlobalEmail is X, with an agent whose OwnLogin is X and Subagents > 0:
- `For(all, null).Agents` contains that agent.
- The global tab''s `TabActivity` is Busy.', '2026-11-02T18:22:09Z');

