**What happened.** C: filled to 1.2 MB.
- Agent-made junk was 27.6 GB in %TEMP%\claude, mostly one live session''s scratch copies of an Unreal project (14k build intermediates, four 2.3 GB PCHs).
- Visual Studio installer leftovers took another 9.2 GB.
- The pagefile grew to 43 GB under memory pressure from parallel game players, builds and soaks.
- The existing `--disk-warn-gb`/`--disk-critical-gb` settings only alert.

**Acceptance**
- **New global setting** `orchestrator settings --disk-cleanup-gb <GB>`, default 30, 0 = off, shown in `orchestrator settings`.
  - The daemon checks it.
  - So does an existing global hook (e.g. context-gate on SessionStart/SubagentStop), cached so it runs at most once a minute, so cleanup happens without the dashboard open.
- **Below the threshold, delete only agent-owned junk**, oldest first, until free space reaches the threshold + 10 GB:
  1. `%TEMP%\claude\<project>\<session>` folders whose session is no longer live.
  2. In live sessions: scratchpad build trees and snapshots not written for 2h+ (`Intermediate/`, `obj/`, `bin/`, `Library/`, `*.pch`, archive snapshot copies).
  3. Tool worktrees under `D:\Projects\MindAttic.worktrees` that are already flagged stale.
- **Never delete:**
  - running agents'' task `.output` files
  - anything modified in the last 15 min
  - user files, or temp files no agent made. Report those in the alert instead (e.g. "VS installer leftovers 9.2 GB in %TEMP%").
- **Log and alert:** log every deletion to the orchestrator data dir, and send a Psst alert with GB freed and what remains big (pagefile/hiberfil).
- **Tests** for the selection rules.', '2026-11-05T17:58:32Z');
