Ryan (2026-11-05): "make sure you delete temp files if the folder created date is X in the past, meaning only keep data for an adjustable period where X is 48 hours default settings global."

Today `DiskCleanup` (M.ORCH-T1449) only acts when %TEMP%''s drive falls under `--disk-cleanup-gb`. `%TEMP%\claude` held 1.1 GB on 2026-11-05 with plenty of free space, so nothing was removed. Ryan wants retention by age as well, whatever the free space.

## Acceptance

- New global setting `orchestrator settings --temp-retention-hours <H>`. The default is 48 and 0 turns it off. It is stored beside `DiskCleanupGb` in `OrchestratorSettings` and `OrchestratorVaultSettings`, and shown in the settings summary.
- The daemon runs the age pass about once an hour, whatever the free space, off the tick thread, the way `CleanDiskIfLow` runs.
- `orchestrator disk-cleanup` (which the context gate also runs when no daemon is up) runs the same pass, and `--dry-run` lists what it would delete.
- **What is deleted:** session folders `%TEMP%\claude\<project>\<session-guid>` whose folder **creation time** is more than H hours ago and whose CLI is not live (`LiveSessionIds`). The whole folder is deleted, `tasks` included. A `<project>` folder left empty afterwards is deleted too.
- **Live sessions older than H:** the session folder is kept, so the running CLI does not break. Scratchpad entries created more than H hours ago that nothing has written for `ScratchQuiet` are deleted.
- **Safety, unchanged from T1449:**
  - only session-GUID folders are touched; `bash-edit-diff` and the bundled caches are never touched
  - nothing written in the last `Recent` is deleted
  - reparse points are not followed
  - tool worktrees are never deleted
  - every deletion is appended to `disk-cleanup.log`
- Unit tests for the pure planning step: a folder at H-1h is kept; at H+1h and not live it is deleted; at H+1h and live only old scratch goes; with H=0 nothing is deleted.
- Update the agent-standard "Clean up after yourself" section to name the setting.', '2026-11-06T04:45:32Z');

