1. CutoffAlerts.cs:43 sends the weekly-crossing alert only when !allowedPastWeek, but LoginLocks.AutoLock now locks regardless of org allow (epic M.ORCH-T2108 decision). An allowed login gets locked with no alert/Psst/toast. Fix: alert on the weekly crossing regardless of the allowance; update the class summary (17-19).
2. LoginLock.cs ~184: Unlock records UnlockedInWeek only for weekly-cutoff locks. Manually locking a login already past its cutoff, then unlocking, re-locks it on the next tick via AutoLock. Fix: Unlock takes the login''s current week reset (optional) and records it whatever the reason, so an owner unlock always holds for the rest of that week. Update callers (OrgUnlockCommand, ToggleLockCommand) to pass it if they have it.
3. LoginLock.cs ~136: UnlockedThisWeek compares WeekResetUtc with exact DateTime equality; statusline vs meter-probe resets can differ by seconds, so an unlock is forgotten. Fix: match within the tolerance the code uses elsewhere (SignInState.Same, or under 1h).
4. Add a public LoginLocks.InvalidateLiveCache() (the WPF side needs to clear the ~10s LiveLocked cache after a local Lock/Unlock or a pushed login-locks state), and make LoadBook also treat a busy-database DbException as unreadable.
5. UsageCutoff.cs:44 DefaultFiveHourPercent = 96 but the live 5-hour default (OrchestratorSettings.PaceTargetPercent) is 98 (M.ORCH-T1750; owner''s rule is 98% of 5h, 90% of the week). Fix the constant to 98 (or derive it from OrchestratorSettings'' default) and any test pinned to 96.
6. Docs: LoginLock.cs:62-63 still says auto-lock is separate; replace the placeholder summaries in LoginLock.cs and UsageCutoff.cs ("Loads.", "Custom.", "Text.", "Gets or sets the ...") with what each member means.

Outcome: LoginLockTests/CutoffAlertsTests cover 1-3; build clean.', '2026-11-24T07:25:47Z');

1. AccountMove.cs:182-198 MoveAsync only checks the target is signed in, not locked: `orchestrator move <repo> --account <locked>` (and the dashboard Move to, and --global when the global email is locked) moves a CLI onto a locked login. Fix: refuse with LoginLocks.Refusal(...) after normalizing the target.
2. AccountRebalancer.cs:458 (writes at 467/486/529/563): home = dirOf(f.FromEmail) uses signedIn, which now drops locked logins, so for a CLI that failed over from a now-locked per-CLI login, SetKeyChoice falls back to the GLOBAL ~/.claude.json: the global login loses its API-key approval and the locked login keeps it. Fix: resolve the home config path from mover.Dirs.For(f.FromEmail) when it isn''t in signedIn.
3. AccountRebalancer.cs:542-552 MoveBack sends a failed-over CLI back onto the global login even when its email is locked (FromEmail null, so the guard never fires). Fix: skip move-back when the home login (FromEmail ?? global email) is locked.
