- Built on the official NATS.Net client. Apps never reference NATS types directly.
- `PublishAsync<T>` (JetStream, sets every envelope header, `Nats-Msg-Id` from the caller or UUIDv7).
- `SubscribeAsync<T>(app, handler)`: one durable consumer per subscribing app, explicit ack only after the handler
  returns, bounded redelivery, then dead-letter (design section 8.5); built-in idempotency helper backed by a
  `relay_processed` table the app owns.
- `RequestAsync<TReq,TRes>` with a timeout and a plain-words failure; `ServeAsync` registers a NATS service with stats.
- `KeyValue(bucket)`: get, put, conditional update on revision, watch.
- Connects to the local Relay server with the app''s credential from MindAttic.Vault; reconnects forever with backoff;
  never blocks the app''s own work while disconnected (design section 8.6).
- `AddMindAtticRelay(appName)` for Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.

**Done when**
- Integration tests start a throwaway `nats-server` and cover: publish/subscribe, redelivery after a handler throws,
  dead-letter after N failures, duplicate `Nats-Msg-Id` dropped, request timeout message, KV conditional update
  conflict, reconnect after the server restarts.

