One native WPF app, **MindAttic.Vault.Desktop**, never network-exposed, is the only place any MindAttic app''s settings or keys are edited. No web-hosted settings UI is ever built.

- **Profiles**: `Desktop` (local AppData files) and `Azure` (App Configuration holds every name and plain value; Key Vault holds secret values via Key Vault references). Same tabs and fields in every Profile; Load/Save on Azure replaces the Azure portal. More Profiles later = one new class.
- **App tabs are generated** from each app''s `settings.manifest.json` (written from `[SettingsApp]`/`[Setting]`/`[UsesCredential]` attributes on the app''s settings class). No app UI code runs inside Desktop.
- **Name/Value everywhere**, IConfiguration-style: `{AppId}:{Property}`, `Llm:{provider}:ApiKeys:{keyName}`, `{AppId}:Keys:{provider}` = ordered key names (first = active, rest = fallbacks).
- **Keys**: one shared named list per provider (provider catalog with aliases), managed only on the Keys tab; apps pick an active key + fallbacks on their own tab; no per-app secret copies (existing scoped copies are imported).
- **Failover**: `KeySelector` tries active then fallbacks; 401/403 marks a key failed, 429 cools it down; key health is shared machine-wide and shown in Desktop.
- **First run**: each app seeds defaults from its settings class (`LoadOrSeed`); new users only bring keys (Get Started checklist).
- Local keys stay plain text (no DPAPI). Per-user / per-universe / CMS data stays in its app.
- Remembered state, audit log, single instance (`--app <id>` from each app''s cog), folder-ACL check, `MaSecretBox`.

Delivered together, built in dependency order: Vault core → Components → Vault.Desktop → Azure Profile → every app. Every child ticket is linked `part-of` this one.', '2026-10-31T14:44:58Z');
