2. Cross-login messaging (/research, member-contact): check whether MindAttic.Orchestrator''s ''orchestrator org start <repo> <who> --prompt'' mechanism (referenced in AGENTS.md''s /research section) is already CLI-agnostic -- i.e. does it launch whatever AgentProviderRegistry.RunCommand the target login''s chosen provider actually is (Claude, Codex, Kimi, or agy), not just Claude? If so, the ''start the work under another login'' half of /research may already work cross-CLI today; only the final ''message the sending session back in real time'' step is Claude-SDK-specific (SendMessage/ListAgents). Investigate whether a simpler, generic notify-back exists or can be built (a ticket note the asker polls, a completion marker file, anything that doesn''t require Claude''s own session-to-session messaging) so the asking CLI doesn''t need Claude''s SDK to eventually learn the research finished -- even if it''s not as instant as SendMessage''s live push. Report precisely which half is genuinely bridgeable and which, if any, remains architecturally impossible (e.g. truly synchronous reach-into-another-running-session''s-conversation, as opposed to async completion signaling).
3. Artifact''s real job is ''produce a page the user/team can view and share.'' This workspace ALREADY has a provider-neutral mechanism for exactly that: the GitHub Pages docs-site pipeline documented in AGENTS.md (''Docs site: every repo on GitHub Pages (HOUSE-LAW-14)'', MindAttic.Agency/shared/docs-site/). Confirm it is genuinely usable by any CLI (it''s just PowerShell + git + GitHub Actions, no Claude-specific step), then explicitly document it in AGENTS.md and the relevant ability files as the cross-CLI equivalent for ''I need to publish something shareable'' -- update any ability whose claude-only reason was ''needs Artifact'' to point at this instead, if the need it actually serves is ''make a shareable page'' rather than something Artifact-specific (live comments, runtime capabilities, in-chat preview) that genuinely has no non-Claude.ai equivalent -- be honest about which parts of Artifact''s feature set (plain static page vs. its live/interactive runtime capabilities) the docs-site pipeline can and cannot replace.

Update shared/abilities/*.md frontmatter and docs/hook-contract-matrix.md (or a new docs/claude-only-abilities.md if that reads better) with the final, precise verdict per item: TRUE-EQUIVALENT-BUILT, PARTIAL-EQUIVALENT (name exactly what''s covered vs not), or CONFIRMED-ARCHITECTURALLY-IMPOSSIBLE (with the specific technical reason, not just ''no SDK feature named this'').', '2026-11-06T17:26:51Z');

Finding: this needs the SAME session to produce new, visible output on its own timer with no keystroke. Claude Code''s native ScheduleWakeup tool genuinely does that (it''s what /loop dynamic mode already relies on). The portable schedule-wakeup ability (schedule-wakeup.ps1) does NOT serve this despite being the provider-agnostic mechanism: it re-invokes a brand-new non-interactive process logging to its own file, never the live tab anyone is watching (confirmed by reading the script - the claude/codex/kimi/agy invocation lines never pass a resume/session flag). AGENTS.md already documents ScheduleWakeup as having no Codex/Kimi/agy equivalent (MAT-T93/94/95/96 section) - this rule inherits that same Claude-only gap honestly rather than faking it with the portable mechanism.

Implementation: a new AGENTS.md house-rule section (near the pacing rule) instructing Claude Code sessions to self-schedule via ScheduleWakeup while background work is outstanding and the user is quiet, printing the bulleted status each time it fires if both conditions still hold, and stopping the moment either breaks. The interval is a small shared config file, shared/config/idle-status.json ({intervalMinutes: 5}), read by the rule with a hardcoded 5-minute fallback.', '2026-11-07T02:57:27Z');

