Principle: the closer a CorpoNation''s business is to the ground (security, policing, utilities, food, freight, labor, heavy industry), the lower its Tier. A parent always sits one Tier above the subsidiaries it owns (law 01a18e63-cae7: tiers on tiers are one family, parent on top), so ArcSec and Halcyon Civil Security are Tier 1 and their parents Tier 2.

Work: write a Tier onto every GLMZ CorpoNation record (offstage ones such as the Alaska Native corporations and the orbital firms get none); brands and subsidiaries take a Tier at or below their parent.
Known conflicts to fix in the same pass: Libation Corporation''s record claims "Tier 5 charter status" (Tier 5 is a rumor); several brand records still use "Zone 1-9" numbering (the world facts forbid zone numbers).', '2026-10-30T19:59:57Z');

Schema:
1. Tier as a real field on CorpoNations and subsidiaries (the unused Tier column, made an int 1-4; the mapper stops blanking it; `tier` writable through set_entity_fields; shown in list_corponations). Tier 5 is refused (a rumor no one holds).
2. CorporateOwnerships: owner (a CorpoNation) -> owned (any entity: CorpoNation, subsidiary, faction, place, asset), kind, stake, since, notes. No cycles; a tiered owner sits above a tiered holding (parent on top). Backfilled from Subsidiary.ParentCorponationId.
3. CorporateForces: a CorpoNation''s own military forces (name, kind, optional entity such as Halcyon Civil Security, strength, notes).
4. A hierarchy service: chain up to the ultimate parent, the tree down to ground level, the forces a CorpoNation can call up (its own plus every descendant''s), and an audit (tier-order violations, cycles, untiered CorpoNations).
5. CLI `prose --corp ...` and MCP tools for all of it; unit tests; docs/SCHEMA.md.

Then the data: a Tier on every GLMZ CorpoNation, the ownership rows down to the ground, and each one''s forces.', '2026-10-30T20:08:37Z');
- "Tier N augmented" on executives (Arcturus, Helix, Ringo, Tessera, Zheng-dao, OmniPro and the offstage Alaska corporations): a neuretic grade, now Standard, Extend, Prime or Atlas.
- Security divisions named "Tier 1/2/3" (Ringo''s Greens/Grays/Blacks, Tessera''s Whites/Prisms/Veil, Helix''s Greens/Shields/Caduceus, Zheng-dao''s Sentinels/Stormfront/Lattice, Cook Inlet''s police): rename to "Line 1/2/3" or by their names alone.
- Libation Corporation''s "Tier 5 charter status" and its dining model by patron Tier: Tier 5 is a rumor; Tier 1 patrons are millionaires now, and its cheapest chain serves the untiered Seams.
- Numbered zones (the author: "Zones are old terminology, GLMZ isn''t divided into zones"): Axiom BioNanics ("Z1 through Z5"), Cordon Freight ("Zone 4 disposition"), Ironmoth, Lattice Systems, Mekong Form, Meridian Provisional Solutions ("Zone 7"), Oma Nano-Therapeutics ("Z2"), Orison Neuretics, Steadfast Medical Systems, Thornback, Thornfield, Velasca, Wyvern Arms. Replace each with a real place, a tier, or the Seams.
