Cause: UniverseGraphService keys nodes by Slugify(Name) (PRS-T916). 55 live file entities (e.g. pilot ''Bertrand Esposito'', ship ''MV Swiftsure'') share a name with an entity the same push retired; the merged graph node carries status ''archived'', so kit.py leak() puts it in `ignored` and drops every edge touching it, then reports the live entity''s edges as missing. All 161 missing edges have an ignored endpoint; none is truly absent.

Fix options: key graph nodes by entity id (PRS-T916), or have leak() ignore an archived node only when no live file entity has its name slug.

Test: leak() on a file with a live entity named like a retired one passes when the snapshot holds its edges.', '2026-11-07T23:39:48Z');

## Context
Author, 2026-11-16: the one thing GLMZ is missing is **cyberpunk cosmic horror**. Right now Schisms are only
storms: geometry breaks, a 19 Hz hum, Kentucky lost, Rome locked, and the Lure, the Counter and Tequenica.
They must also be **passages**. Things come *through* from an infinite range of dimensions:
- biological, mechanical, post-technological, geometric, energy, informational;
- most die within moments in our physics;
- some live just long enough to kill;
- a few find our world bearable and plunder it;
- some are docile and become part of the city''s New Weird;
- people can be pulled back *in*.

There is also a stunted adjacent shortcut universe (the author''s "Dragon/Weyr Space") to explore. Together these form a
**pillar beside CorpoNations, nanotech, cyberware and gene mods**: just ANOTHER thing GLMZ residents live
with. It gives heroes an enemy that isn''t a human, a robot or a lazy "escaped lab experiment".

**Author''s answers, 2026-11-16:**
- The shortcut space gets a **GLMZ-native name** ("Weyr" reads as Pern). I''ll propose options in the bible.
- Depth: **every book + 4-6 set-pieces**.
- **Pause for the author''s review of the bible before any prose is spliced.**

**The author''s design rules:**
- No New England, fish or tentacle Cthulhu.
- No "million eyes + giant claws", and no perfect predator that would end the world.
- **Respect biology.** Every arrival answers: what did it live on back home, and why does it die here (or not)?
- Arrivals never feel trite, because they are studied, catalogued and harvested.
- The Cabal knows about them all, and the CorpoNations are fascinated.

**Existing canon this must fit:**
- **GLMZ.md:530-577:**
  - The Cabal''s corridor caused "The Schism".
  - The Interstice is the substrate.
  - "There is no inside": you can be adjacent to a Schism or pass through one, never be inside it.
  - AAMA Class 1-5; 19 Hz base tone; micro-schism pebbles.
  - "Bleed" is reserved for neuretics.
  - The Cabal, book 23, closes only the lake taps.
- **WORLD.md:105-136:** **a schism has no intent**, and the intelligences on the far side are separate beings. Arrivals respect this: the rift is still weather, and what falls out of it has the wants.
- **Phase 1 dimensional ticket T484:** "never the explanation". Arrivals get catalogued, but the rift''s cause is never explained on the page.
- **BIBLE.md SS-LAW-25 (LOCKED):** the Superminds-caused-it secret stays Kyle''s burden and the BCODA reveal. No arrival scene leaks it.
- **BIBLE.md SS-LAW-15:** Kyle reads micro-schisms 4-8 s early. That is the human end of the forecasting science.
- Machines are never alive, so mechanical arrivals are machines, still running, never "life".
- Species stays at its five rows; arrivals are not a sixth species.
- Law 01a109a0''s "schisms like predators waiting for a straggler" now contradicts the no-intent rule. Fix it by saying the predator is what comes *through*, not the rift itself.

## Approach (standing GLMZ process: ticket for every step, write before read, rulings in the Hub, hand splices)

### Step 0: Ticket
One root ticket for the Schism Passages pillar, plus child tickets per phase and per book (`glmz-vision`, `seq:` ordered,
`book:<slug>`). No work happens without a ticket.

### Phase 0: Rules (`record_ruling`, universe glmz; prohibitions only get regex patterns)
1. **LAW, passages.**
   - Schisms are also passages. Arrivals come from any reach of the Interstice.
   - Most die within minutes (wrong pressure, gravity, chirality, base frequency, temperature).
   - Survival is bounded by a radius around the rift where some home physics persists.
   - People and things can be taken back through.
   - The rift keeps no intent; arrivals have their own.
2. **LAW, the biology test.** Every named arrival carries four facts: home niche, food or energy source, cause of death here (or why
   it survives), and what people harvest or fear. No apex super-predators, and no tentacle or eye-cluster shorthand.
3. **LAW, the eight kinds.** Every arrival is one of these:
   - biological;
   - mechanical (machines, not alive);
   - post-technological;
   - geometric cross-section (a 4D thing seen as disconnected pulsing blobs; fits "no inside");
   - energy or field;
   - informational/memetic;
   - colonial (organized takers and plunderers, alien in motive, never cartoon-evil);
   - docile/ambient (the New Weird people live with).
4. **LAW, the shortcut universe.**
   - It is a stunted universe mapped 1:1 onto ours, so tunnelling through it shortens distance.
   - It has native life, and some arrivals are backwash from traffic through it.
   - The hazard is misrouting, Aquila-Rift style (captives kept comfortable).
   - The name is held until the author picks one.
