The figures (scripts/figures, 23 SVGs in figures/) were blocked from the PDF and DOCX because MindAttic.Export dropped images. That gate is cleared: MindAttic.Export 5.2.0 (M.EXPT-T31, commit f78cfec on main) embeds them. scripts/export.ps1 runs the CLI from ..\MindAttic.Export source, so the next export picks it up with no package change.

## What the exporter does now
- A paragraph that is **only** a Markdown image is a figure: `![Alt text](../figures/fig-02-conditions-and-dependencies.svg)`. An image inside a sentence is still dropped.
- Relative paths resolve against the directory of the chapter `.md` file that contains them (chapters/ -> use `../figures/...`). Absolute paths, `file:` and base64 `data:` URIs also work; `http(s):` is never downloaded.
- PDF draws SVG as vector. DOCX stores the SVG (vector in Word 2016+) with a PNG fallback. PNG/JPEG/GIF are embedded as is.
- Size comes from the SVG''s own `width`/`height` (any CSS unit, e.g. `width="6in" height="3.3in"`), else its viewBox in CSS px. Never scaled up; scaled down to fit the text block (Letter: 6.5in wide, about 7.2in tall). So the planned physical inch sizes in svg.py are honoured exactly.
- Captions are not generated: write the APA caption as ordinary paragraphs above the image (`**Figure N**` line, then `*Title*` line). The List of Figures is also yours to write.
- An image that cannot be found prints `[Figure: alt]` in DOCX/PDF/TXT/EPUB instead of vanishing, so check the export for that string. EPUB does not embed figures yet (placeholder only).

## Acceptance
- svg.py rescale (8-10pt type at print size, physical inch sizes) done; the smoke export showed note lines overflowing the right edge and overlapping labels in fig-02 and fig-05 at current sizes.
- Each figure placed in its chapter with an APA caption; List of Figures added.
- Re-export via scripts/export.ps1; no `[Figure:` placeholder in the .txt; figures visible in the PDF and the DOCX (open in Word).
- Copy .pdf/.docx to exports/ and .md to docs/ as usual, and make sure Pages serves figures/ at the path the .md references.', '2026-11-03T04:55:11Z');

