Gadfly''s owner asked (GAD-T414 research) whether a faster STT alternative to ElevenLabs Scribe exists. Prose
(D:\Projects\MindAttic\Prose, src/Prose.Core/Services/Discussion/SpeechService.cs) already uses Groq''s hosted
Whisper endpoint (`whisper-large-v3-turbo`) as its primary speech-to-text provider, with OpenAI `whisper-1` as
fallback. Prose''s own code comment calls Groq "the fastest hosted transcription available", at about $0.04/hour
(vs OpenAI whisper-1 at $0.006/min = $0.36/hour). Both are batch/per-utterance (no streaming partials), and both
speak the same OpenAI-compatible `multipart/form-data` "audio/transcriptions" REST shape, so Prose''s SpeechService
posts to both providers with one shared code path, differing only in base URL, model name and API key.

This library''s `OpenAiWhisperRecognizer` (src/MindAttic.SpeechRecognition/Providers/OpenAI/OpenAiWhisperRecognizer.cs)
already implements exactly that OpenAI-compatible shape: `OpenAiWhisperOptions.BaseUri` (default
`https://api.openai.com/`), `.Model` (default `whisper-1`), and a request built with
`new Uri(_opt.BaseUri, "v1/audio/transcriptions")`. Groq''s OpenAI-compatible endpoint is
`https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/audio/transcriptions`, i.e. `BaseUri = https://api.groq.com/openai/`,
`Model = whisper-large-v3-turbo` would hit the same request path almost unchanged. But doing this today from a
consuming app (e.g. Gadfly) by just repointing the existing "OpenAI" provider''s BaseUri/Model would be a misnomer:
`OpenAiWhisperRecognizer.ProviderName` is hard-coded to `"openai-whisper"`, its SessionId prefix is `"whisper-"`,
its auth-failure message says "No OpenAI API key is configured (expected MindAttic:Vault:LLM:openai:apiKey...)",
and `RecognizerFactory` reads the key from `MindAttic:Vault:LLM:openai:apiKey` specifically -- all of which would
mislabel a Groq-backed session as OpenAI and collide with a real OpenAI key/config if an app wants both available
as distinct choices (e.g. Gadfly''s `Fallback` provider already chains ElevenLabs -> OpenAI; a third choice should
not quietly share OpenAI''s identity and vault key).

## Acceptance

- A new `Providers/Groq/GroqWhisperRecognizer.cs` (or a thin specialization reusing the OpenAI request-building code,
  refactored into a shared base if that''s cleaner) with `ProviderName => "groq-whisper"`, default
