Cause: Tutor.Core/Services/EmbeddingService.cs CreateBatches estimates tokens as text.Length / CharsPerToken against MaxTokensPerBatch = 250000; dictionary-style text tokenizes far denser than 4 chars/token. Also one failed batch drops every batch''s embeddings for the resource.

Fix: batch by a conservative estimate (e.g. 2.5 chars/token or a count cap like 512 inputs/batch), make the cap a Vault setting, and on a 400 for size split the batch in half and retry. Then re-embed the TUT-T50 dictionary (and Complete Shakespeare if it also failed) courses. Not fixed in TUT-T50 because EmbeddingService.cs is in another agent''s working area (TUT-T52/T59).', '2026-11-19T22:49:01Z');

Cause: `LocalQuizController.GenerateQuestionsAsync` falls through to `QuizGenerationService.GenerateAsync(course.ConceptMapCollectionId, ...)`, which calls `ConceptMapStorageService.LoadAsync("collection_<courseId>")`. That id names a ConceptMapCollection in `ConceptMaps/collections/`, not a ConceptMap, so it is always null (log: "ConceptMap file not found ... collection_<id>.json"), and `QuizTab.StartQuiz` shows nothing when the session is null. Also "N concepts learned" counts names (e.g. "All Concepts") that match no concept id.

Also seen online: lesson replies render placeholder suggested questions ("First/Second/Third specific question about All Concepts?"), and a restored lesson shows the internal "IMPORTANT CONTEXT - SPIRAL LEARNING" prompt as the user''s message.

