A keyframe (the save graph) restored mid-battle re-simulates bit-identically for a while, then diverges the moment a carrier fighter works a flight deck. Found by the US-T99 rewind probe: `Bench.Rewind.exe --scenario battle --rewind-probe --rewind-then-warp 0 --ticks 7000` restores at ticks 2333 and 4666; both match the live digest at restore and +60 ticks, both diverge at exactly tick 5229 (first differing line: a Fighter''s pos/vel in Sol''s battle). The battle scenario at its own warp 2 happens to pass. The same loss hits every ordinary save/load and co-op resync taken while a fighter holds a deck visit.

## Cause
A carrier''s `FlightDeck` objects live in `FlightDecks::Of`''s static table (Combat/FlightDecks.cpp ~126-171; C#''s ConditionalWeakTable), which saves deliberately skip (docs/PERSISTENCE.md section 11). But `FighterState.Deck` (a `DeckVisit`) references its `FlightDeck`, so that deck object is saved and loaded. After a load, `FlightDecks::Of(carrier)` finds no table entry and builds new decks, so the fighter''s visit points at an orphan copy that the carrier no longer runs (graph diff at tick 5228 live vs replayed: `DeckVisit:Deck` points at a different entry, the replay has 2 extra entries). Deck state (`Final`, `Aboard`, `NextLaunch`) then splits between the two copies.

## Fix direction
After a load, seed the deck table from the loaded decks (an SG_LOADED hook on Battle/World that registers every `FlightDeck` reached through `DeckVisit`s under its `Carrier`, in the order Build makes them), or make the decks part of the saved carrier. Must keep the 5 Bench digests.

## Test
`tools/build-bench-cpp.ps1 -Rewind` then `Bench.Rewind.exe --scenario battle --rewind-probe --rewind-then-warp 0 --ticks 7000` reports `determinism: ALL MATCH`.', '2026-11-05T09:30:16Z');

So a bounty, the crimes and the standing earned in one body follow the SpaceGod into the next. A pirate captain''s piracy makes a freighter it takes next "WANTED", and patrols interdict it.

**Cause.** This is a direct port of the Unity game, where the player *was* one pilot. It conflicts with the design rule from US-T135, US-T137, US-T138 and US-T140: the player is never one particular pilot. Reputation, crimes and bounties belong to the embodied pilot or hull and stay with them when the SpaceGod leaves. Only Influence (US-T140, `SpaceGodInfluence`) belongs to the SpaceGod.

**Fix.** Remove the global record:
- `RecordOf`/`FindRecord(PilotedShip)` return the hull''s own captain record, so a piloted hull is booked like any other.
- Player-flown units book to their hull''s captain record.
- Patrol hails, bounty hunters, contract eligibility, smuggling surcharges and lane pickets read the record of the hull now held (`RecordOf(world->PilotedShip)`), not a global one.
- EventDirector''s player standing becomes the held hull''s faction standing.
- The HUD''s "WANTED" reads the held hull''s record.

Save compatibility: older saves carry `Player`. On load, fold its bounties into the record of the hull piloted at save time (or drop them), and keep the field optional.

**Test.** Commit piracy at a pirate''s helm, release, and take a lawful freighter. The freighter is not wanted, no patrol interdicts it, and the pirate captain''s record still holds the bounty. A Bench run is unchanged because no player flies there.

Found while doing US-T140 (Embody limits and Influence). It is not fixed there because the sweep touches about 13 call sites across Law, Outlaws, Contracts, Smuggling, War, Events and the HUD, plus a save migration.', '2026-11-05T18:18:42Z');

This was not shown in game. The US-T151 checks proved only the heir-ahead half: the heir starts ahead and pulls away, and nothing came near the held hull in either run. An iso-only probe that steered the held hull at 0.3 km/s onto a flagship''s planned track never closed: the range grew, because the probe''s velocity override did not survive the frame (the helm''s ENGINES STOP and flight model). So no free ship was ever threatened.

Verify: hold a capital at rest on a scheduled ship''s track, or fly slowly at a parked flagship, and log Fleet::EvasionOf and EvadingFrom for it. Expect a sidestep that grows from 0 km and a closest pass of at least the safe berth, with no collision. If it does not, fix it.', '2026-11-06T05:52:31Z');

Cause: FighterAI::Wingman skips Formations::BreakTarget whenever the lead is on an attack run against a strafeable capital (US-T180''s swarm), and FighterAI::Lead puts a fighter lead on that attack run straight from Approach at any range. So a squadron going for a capital never holds its shape on the way in, and a wingman jumped by an enemy fighter (JumpedKm) keeps strafing.

Fix: the wingmen split off onto their own strafing runs only once the lead is within Formations::StrafeBreakKm of the hull, holding the (attack-run loosened) formation until then; and the break check runs during a strafe too, so a wingman jumped by an enemy fighter breaks into a dogfight and rejoins once it is over.

Test: sg.Squadron logs every wingman''s slot error and broken state each second.', '2026-11-06T14:02:40Z');
As a player I want SpaceGod to make sound, so that battles, flight and menus feel alive. Today the game is silent: there is no audio asset under Cpp/Content or Shared/Plugins/SpaceGodRender/Content, no USoundBase/UAudioComponent use anywhere in Cpp/Source, and the only audio setting is `audio.masterVolume` (Cpp/Source/SpaceGod/EngineSettings.cpp), which sets AudioListener::volume with nothing playing. The other audio tickets build on this one.

## Acceptance
- [ ] An audio layer in the Runtime (e.g. Cpp/Source/SpaceGod/Audio/) that plays 2D and 3D positional one-shots and loops through Unreal''s audio engine, with a sound class/submix per bus: Master, Music, Effects, Interface, Ambience.
- [ ] Settings > Audio gains Music, Effects, Interface and Ambience volumes (RangeSetting, saved to the profile like audio.masterVolume); the -muted CLI mute (SessionAudio) still silences everything.
- [ ] A small set of CC0/royalty-free starter sounds imported under Cpp/Content/SpaceGod/Audio and listed in docs/ThirdPartyArt.md with licences.
- [ ] Each co-op peer plays its own sounds locally (nothing enters the lockstep frames); Bench digests unchanged.
- [ ] --headless / -RenderOffscreen runs work with no audio device.', '2026-11-08T06:07:30Z');
As a pilot in a fight I want to hear every gun, missile, beam and impact around me. The Core already raises the cues: Battle.cpp:3279 calls WeaponSystems::CueFx when WeaponSystems::SoundHook() is set (SpaceGodCore/Combat/WeaponSystems.cpp:169-250), but nothing in Cpp/Source/SpaceGod sets SoundHook, so the cues go nowhere. Needs the audio foundation ticket.

## Acceptance
- [ ] The Runtime binds WeaponSystems::SoundHook and plays a positional sound per WeaponSoundCue: distinct fire sounds per weapon kind (gun, vulcan spin-up, railgun, laser/phaser, plasma, tachyon lance, missile/hive/rocket/torpedo launch, flak, EMP, mine), plus shield hit, hull hit, subsystem destroyed and ship explosion.
- [ ] Attenuation by battle-space distance from the listener (embodied unit or camera) and a voice cap per kind, nearest first, so a fleet battle does not clip.
- [ ] Far from the fight in the free SpaceGod view, sounds are muffled/filtered rather than silent or full-volume.
- [ ] sg.BigBattle and the dogfight demo are audible; Bench digests unchanged.', '2026-11-08T06:07:42Z');
As a pilot I want my craft''s engines, thrusters, boost, cruise drive, lane ride and FTL spool to be audible, and warnings to sound. US-T170 asked for engine audio scaled by mass, but nothing plays sound. SpaceGodCore/Combat/DriveRegime.h:34/68 already exposes one cue per regime change "for the cues (the screen''s flash, a sound)". Needs the audio foundation ticket.

## Acceptance
- [ ] The embodied craft plays an engine loop whose pitch/volume follow throttle and thrust, scaled by mass class (fighter whine to capital rumble); RCS puffs when manoeuvring jets fire (Views/RcsJets, Views/HullThrusters know when).
- [ ] Boost, flip-and-burn, drift, cruise spool/engage/drop-out, lane enter/exit, gate jump and FTL spool/jump each have a sound, driven from DriveRegime cues.
- [ ] Alerts on the Interface bus: missile lock warning, incoming missile, shields down, hull critical, propellant low, self-destruct countdown, Bio Mass contact.
- [ ] Nearby AI ships'' engines are audible in passing at close range.', '2026-11-08T06:07:43Z');
As a player I want music that follows what is happening: calm between the planets, tense in a fight, unsettling in the void as dread builds, and a theme on the main menu. There is no music in the repo. Needs the audio foundation ticket (Music bus and volume).

